akreddy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/b07603507aad9679fa7c8c3eb39d263e334431d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:22:07Z","email":"DGORISI@ibs-b.hu","name":"thedeepakreddy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:22:07Z","email":"DGORISI@ibs-b.hu","name":"thedeepakreddy"},"message":"feat: add background ML service wake button, drop shut-down Gemini model\n\nThe Python ML service runs on a Render free instance, which spins down after\n~15 minutes idle. The next request then pays a cold start - measured at 41s\nagainst the live deployment - which previously landed on whoever happened to\nkick off a training run.\n\nAdd a header toggle that pays that cost up front, in the background:\n\n- POST /api/ml-service/wake probes the service''s /health endpoint, polling\n  patiently through the cold start (20s per probe, 120s total budget) and\n  returning only status metadata. Server-side on purpose: the browser cannot\n  probe the ML host directly without CORS on it, and proxying keeps the\n  service URL out of the client bundle. Nothing is rendered to the user.\n- GET /api/ml-service/status is a cheap no-retry probe the UI polls every\n  10 minutes while the toggle is on, so the instance stays warm.\n- MLServiceWakeButton drives both, with idle/waking/online/error states. It\n  aborts in-flight requests and clears its timers on unmount and on toggle-off.\n\nML_SERVICE_URL still wins when configured (production, docker, local uvicorn);\nthe public Render URL is the fallback so the button is useful when the app runs\nlocally without an ML service of its own.\n\nAlso fix the Gemini fallback chain. gemini-2.0-flash was shut down on\n2026-06-01, so every call to it failed and only burned a retry cycle before the\nchain gave up. Replace it with gemini-3.8-flash (current latest) and\ngemini-3.6-flash (Google''s named replacement for 2.0-flash), keeping\ngemini-2.5-flash last as the widely-provisioned safety net. The app passes no\ntemperature/topK/topP/thinkingBudget, so the Gemini 3 family''s stricter\nsampling-parameter rules do not affect these calls.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44752038a0d9d34e85db58657a9bae536aef8c18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/trees/44752038a0d9d34e85db58657a9bae536aef8c18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/commits/b07603507aad9679fa7c8c3eb39d263e334431d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203024836?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy","id":203024836,"login":"thedeepakreddy","node_id":"U_kgDODBnpxA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakreddy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedeepakre