-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/723fd64f44f16eaa4e84cf6aeb3b55257f705a8c","node_id":"C_kwDOSoFmP9oAKDcyM2ZkNjRmNDRmMTZlYWE0ZTg0Y2Y2YWViM2I1NTI1N2Y3MDVhOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009","sha":"e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a","sha":"853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a"}],"sha":"723fd64f44f16eaa4e84cf6aeb3b55257f705a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/723fd64f44f16eaa4e84cf6aeb3b55257f705a8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:22:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:22:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: deep code review - correctness, security, and stability fixes\n\nA full pass through the app for bugs found 12 issues; all are fixed and\nverified (tsc, vite build, pytest, ruff all pass):\n\n- ABTestInterpreter: p-value calc ignored the sign of z and used the wrong\n  two-tailed/one-tailed formula direction\n- SmartBoxPlot: early return before a useMemo call violated Rules of Hooks,\n  crashing the chart on empty data\n- csvParser: header dedup could collide two originally-distinct headers onto\n  the same generated name, silently discarding a column''s data\n- MLPipeline: lowercase <cell> in the PCA scatter plot rendered as an inert\n  host element instead of recharts'' <Cell>, breaking cluster coloring\n- server.ts: chat-bot SQL fallback''s UPDATE regex used [^where] (a character\n  class excluding w/h/e/r) instead of stopping at the literal word WHERE,\n  truncating captured values that contained those letters\n- server.ts: Postgres connections accepted any TLS certificate\n  (rejectUnauthorized: false); now verifies real certificates\n- server.ts: removed a dead savedDbConfig module-level variable that held\n  connection strings/credentials in memory with no reader anywhere\n- AssistiveTouchBot: LLM-generated dataset-transform code ran via new\n  Function in the page''s own privileged context - a dataset cell carrying a\n  prompt-injection payload could reach cookies/localStorage/DOM. Now runs\n  inside an isolated, opaque-origin sandboxed iframe\n- DataCleaning: adding/deleting a row didn''t record a CleaningOperation like\n  every other edit, so those edits were invisible to the ETL script exporter\n- mlops_service: choose_positive_label raised an uncaught IndexError when\n  extreme class imbalance collapsed y_train to a single class; now degrades\n  to the existing multi-class metrics path instead of crashing training\n- App.tsx: LoadingScreen''s onComplete was a fresh closure every render,\n  restarting its dismiss timer on any App re-render during the loading window\n- StakeholderDashboard: the Leaflet map was destroyed and rebuilt on every\n  filter change, losing pan/zoom and re-fetching tiles; markers now update\n  in place on a persistent map instance\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb2Ssg7HbHLMqRrGtTEm7f","tree":{"sha":"4bfd2dd7093cb719200af7e61d0341e0bf75511b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/trees/4bfd2dd7093cb719200af7e61d0341e0bf75511b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/commits/853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bfd2dd7093cb719200af7e61d0341e0bf75511b\nparent e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789172557 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789172557 +0000\n\nfix: deep code review - correctness, security, and stability fixes\n\nA full pass through the app for bugs found 12 issues; all are fixed and\nverified (tsc, vite build, pytest, ruff all pass):\n\n- ABTestInterpreter: p-value calc ignored the sign of z and used the wrong\n  two-tailed/one-tailed formula direction\n- SmartBoxPlot: early return before a useMemo call violated Rules of Hooks,\n  crashing the chart on empty data\n- csvParser: header dedup could collide two originally-distinct headers onto\n  the same generated name, silently discarding a column''s data\n- MLPipeline: lowercase <cell> in the PCA scatter plot rendered as an inert\n  host element instead of recharts'' <Cell>, breaking cluster coloring\n- server.ts: chat-bot SQL fallback''s UPDATE regex used [^where] (a character\n  class excluding w/h/e/r) instead of stopping at the literal word WHERE,\n  truncating captured values that contained those letters\n- server.ts: Postgres connections accepted any TLS certificate\n  (rejectUnauthorized: false); now verifies real certificates\n- server.ts: removed a dead savedDbConfig module-level variable that held\n  connection strings/credentials in memory with no reader anywhere\n- AssistiveTouchBot: LLM-generated dataset-transform code ran via new\n  Function in the page''s own privileged context - a dataset cell carrying a\n  prompt-injection payload could reach cookies/localStorage/DOM. Now runs\n  inside an isolated, opaque-origin sandboxed iframe\n- DataCleaning: adding/deleting a row didn''t record a CleaningOperation like\n  every other edit, so those edits were invisible to the ETL script exporter\n- mlops_service: choose_positive_label raised an uncaught IndexError when\n  extreme class imbalance collapsed y_train to a single class; now degrades\n  to the existing multi-class metrics path instead of crashing training\n- App.tsx: LoadingScreen''s onComplete was a fresh closure every render,\n  restarting its dismiss timer on any App re-render during the loading window\n- StakeholderDashboard: the Leaflet map was destroyed and rebuilt on every\n  filter change, losing pan/zoom and re-fetching tiles; markers now update\n  in place on a persistent map instance\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb2Ssg7HbHLMqRrGtTEm7f\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCAdTaQ4\n2L+96cuzv0N7PD+ZTcmiJmjBULnevpXZUFD4C5fJwlk6PcE2Qi30Et04ghUWBRgxxb3HpGgIeDha\nYQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T00:22:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a","node_id":"C_kwDOSoFmP9oAKDg1M2Y4MTIzN2IxZGM5MmMwN2MxMTc0ZjA2MTA5NjU2YWJjY2Y2MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009","sha":"e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/e3a638afc05f221ca0290258b7af5dcadd7ad009"}],"sha":"853f81237b1dc92c07c1174f06109656abccf60a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/D