b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/d2229095dcb4e7f5702b693b586c28149658451b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/a61b9f2afe2e34821ce08bb08ae2fe40eb9af830/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T09:03:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T09:03:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 2: agentic analysis mode (v2, the differentiator)\n\nA real reason -> act -> observe loop, not a single-shot chat wrapper.\n\n- mlops_service: three whitelisted real functions the agent can call, all\n  reusing the exact same training pipeline as /train so an agent-proposed\n  retrain is held to the same standard as any other model in this app -\n  POST /agent/retrain-with-transform (log/sqrt/standardize a real column,\n  then retrain), POST /agent/drop-feature (retrain without one real\n  feature), POST /agent/check-multicollinearity (real VIF per numeric\n  feature via sklearn regression, R^2_i = 1/(1 - VIF_i), not a guessed\n  score). 9 new pytest cases (39/39 total passing) - one of which caught a\n  real bug in this same change: the highRisk flag was backwards for the\n  near-infinite-VIF case, marking the worst multicollinearity as safe.\n- server.ts: POST /api/agent/run orchestrates the loop using Gemini''s\n  function-calling API (FunctionCallingConfigMode.ANY against a fixed\n  allowlist, never free-text command parsing). Gemini gets the champion''s\n  real metrics plus a real EDA summary, proposes one action per turn with\n  a required `reasoning` argument, the real tool result is fed back before\n  the next turn. Hard-capped at 5 steps; also stops on a real result\n  plateau (<1% relative gain) or the agent''s own declare_done call - the\n  stop reason is always explicit, never silent. A worse-than-current\n  result is logged honestly but not adopted as the new working state.\n  Returns a clean, honest 503 when no GEMINI_API_KEY is configured, since\n  this feature (unlike the rest of the app) has no template-narrative\n  fallback - the reasoning itself is the point.\n- New AgentAnalysis.tsx tab in ML Modeling: guardrails (the exact\n  whitelisted function names) stated up front, a step-by-step timeline\n  showing each real before/after metric and whether it was kept or\n  discarded, and the real stop reason - never an opaque black box.\n- README + CASE_STUDY.md updated to document the new mode and its one\n  real remaining nuance (a target-column transform changes the metric''s\n  scale, so the UI flags it rather than treating it as a silent\n  apples-to-apples comparison).\n\nVerified: full pytest suite (39/39) and ruff clean, tsc clean, production\nbuild clean, and the full flow (train a real model -> open the Agentic\nAnalysis tab -> run it) exercised end-to-end against the live app via\nPlaywright, including the honest no-API-key error state. The tool/schema\npayload was also confirmed to reach Gemini''s real API cleanly (rejected\nonly for an invalid key, not a malformed request) - this sandbox has no\nreal GEMINI_API_KEY, so the live multi-turn tool-calling round trip itself\nshould get one real test with a real key before this is fully trusted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb2Ssg7HbHLMqRrGtTEm7f","tree":{"sha":"75c622e7068bbe06882621738195e5547e90bf20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/trees/75c622e7068bbe06882621738195e5547e90bf20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/commits/a61b9f2afe2e34821ce08bb08ae2fe40eb9af830","verification":{"payload":"tree 75c622e7068bbe06882621738195e5547e90bf20\nparent 36aa3e24b3779e4826ed32440ae9f0186012aa02\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785229391 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785229391 +0000\n\nPhase 2: agentic analysis mode (v2, the differentiator)\n\nA real reason -> act -> observe loop, not a single-shot chat wrapper.\n\n- mlops_service: three whitelisted real functions the agent can call, all\n  reusing the exact same training pipeline as /train so an agent-proposed\n  retrain is held to the same standard as any other model in this app -\n  POST /agent/retrain-with-transform (log/sqrt/standardize a real column,\n  then retrain), POST /agent/drop-feature (retrain without one real\n  feature), POST /agent/check-multicollinearity (real VIF per numeric\n  feature via sklearn regression, R^2_i = 1/(1 - VIF_i), not a guessed\n  score). 9 new pytest cases (39/39 total passing) - one of which caught a\n  real bug in this same change: the highRisk flag was backwards for the\n  near-infinite-VIF case, marking the worst multicollinearity as safe.\n- server.ts: POST /api/agent/run orchestrates the loop using Gemini''s\n  function-calling API (FunctionCallingConfigMode.ANY against a fixed\n  allowlist, never free-text command parsing). Gemini gets the champion''s\n  real metrics plus a real EDA summary, proposes one action per turn with\n  a required `reasoning` argument, the real tool result is fed back before\n  the next turn. Hard-capped at 5 steps; also stops on a real result\n  plateau (<1% relative gain) or the agent''s own declare_done call - the\n  stop reason is always explicit, never silent. A worse-than-current\n  result is logged honestly but not adopted as the new working state.\n  Returns a clean, honest 503 when no GEMINI_API_KEY is configured, since\n  this feature (unlike the rest of the app) has no template-narrative\n  fallback - the reasoning itself is the point.\n- New AgentAnalysis.tsx tab in ML Modeling: guardrails (the exact\n  whitelisted function names) stated up front, a step-by-step timeline\n  showing each real before/after metric and whether it was kept or\n  discarded, and the real stop reason - never an opaque black box.\n- README + CASE_STUDY.md updated to document the new mode and its one\n  real remaining nuance (a target-column transform changes the metric''s\n  scale, so the UI flags it rather than treating it as a silent\n  apples-to-apples comparison).\n\nVerified: full pytest suite (39/39) and ruff clean, tsc clean, production\nbuild clean, and the full flow (train a real model -> open the Agentic\nAnalysis tab -> run it) exercised end-to-end against the live app via\nPlaywright, including the honest no-API-key error state. The tool/schema\npayload was also confirmed to reach Gemini''s real API cleanly (rejected\nonly for an invalid key, not a malformed request) - this sandbox has no\nreal GEMINI_API_KEY, so the live multi-turn tool-calling round trip itself\nshould get one real test with a real key before this is fully trusted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb2Ssg7HbHLMqRrGtTEm7f\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFI