.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/36aa3e24b3779e4826ed32440ae9f0186012aa02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:14:16Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:14:16Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 4: recruiter-facing polish, and two real fabrication fixes found along the way\n\n- README rewrite: problem statement, refreshed architecture diagram note,\n  a Live Demo section with a real recorded GIF + screenshots of the actual\n  v1 flow (real EDA, real multi-model AutoML comparison, real SHAP), an\n  expanded honest tech-stack table, and a link to the new CASE_STUDY.md.\n  Docker quickstart section from Phase 3 kept as-is.\n- CASE_STUDY.md: what was actually hard (structurally preventing metric\n  fabrication via schema design, explainable model selection, a real SHAP/\n  numba bug, two bugs the demo recording itself surfaced) and what''s next.\n- Recorded the demo GIF/screenshots by actually running the app end-to-end\n  (Playwright against the real dev server + ml-service, no staging), which\n  surfaced and led to fixing two real, pre-existing bugs: the built-in\n  sample datasets were too small to clear the ml-service''s own 20-row\n  training minimum, and the sequential stage-navigation button relied on\n  hasRunAudit/hasRunEda flags that were never actually set.\n- Also fixed a Vite dev-server bug found in the process: it was watching\n  the runtime-appended deepakllm_training_data.jsonl log file and forcing\n  a disruptive full-page reload (losing app state) on every chat/training\n  interaction; now ignored, and the file is gitignored as the runtime\n  artifact it is.\n- Narrated-vs-computed audit turned up two real fabrications, both fixed\n  rather than just reworded: the Hypothesis Testing Lab generated its\n  p-value with Math.random() (new /hypothesis-test endpoint - real\n  scipy.stats Pearson correlation / Welch''s t-test / one-way ANOVA /\n  chi-squared, chosen from the columns'' actual dtypes, with real column\n  pickers replacing a non-functional \"Auto-detected\" placeholder for\n  custom hypotheses); and the ETL Code Exporter sent a hardcoded fake\n  transformation list to Gemini regardless of what cleaning was actually\n  done (now reads the real, already-tracked CleaningOperation log via a\n  PipelineContext field that existed but was never wired up).\n- 9 new pytest cases for /hypothesis-test (30/30 passing, ruff-clean).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb2Ssg7HbHLMqRrGtTEm7f","tree":{"sha":"147c511eb1676a5648c70139469e70d956e79404","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/trees/147c511eb1676a5648c70139469e70d956e79404"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/commits/36aa3e24b3779e4826ed32440ae9f0186012aa02","verification":{"payload":"tree 147c511eb1676a5648c70139469e70d956e79404\nparent e056f290cf83fa7bd0c9cd5132b0a648f7edda6b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785226456 +0000