github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/4d24ed83d54a13597e8c950b20669f64b5514066","node_id":"C_kwDOSoFmP9oAKDRkMjRlZDgzZDU0YTEzNTk3ZThjOTUwYjIwNjY5ZjY0YjU1MTQwNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/2268eddc46e9f521a4f1eb9676f4c04aa79df6db","sha":"2268eddc46e9f521a4f1eb9676f4c04aa79df6db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/2268eddc46e9f521a4f1eb9676f4c04aa79df6db"}],"sha":"4d24ed83d54a13597e8c950b20669f64b5514066","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/4d24ed83d54a13597e8c950b20669f64b5514066"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/2268eddc46e9f521a4f1eb9676f4c04aa79df6db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:41:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:41:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 1: real AutoML core — multi-model, explainable, real EDA\n\nExtends Phase 0''s real training into an actual AutoML pipeline: multiple\ngenuine candidates compared honestly (losers included), an explainable\nselection rule instead of a black box, real SHAP explainability, and a\nreal server-side EDA endpoint.\n\n- mlops_service/main.py:\n  - AutoML now trains 5 real candidates by default (added\n    GradientBoostingClassifier/Regressor alongside the existing\n    Linear/Logistic, RandomForest, XGBoost, MLP).\n  - Champion selection changed from ranking by a single test-set score to\n    ranking by mean cross-validation score, tie-broken by lower fold-to-fold\n    variance — the exact rule is returned as `selectionReason`, a plain-\n    language string built from the real numbers, not hidden in the backend.\n  - Added real SHAP explainability for the champion model: TreeExplainer for\n    tree-based models, LinearExplainer for linear/logistic, and a bounded\n    generic Explainer for MLP (fixed a real bug where the MLP path passed\n    `.predict` — which returns string class labels — into SHAP''s numeric\n    masking code; classification now correctly explains `.predict_proba`).\n    Values are aggregated back to original column names and returned as\n    `shapImportance`, capped to the top 10 features; failures degrade to\n    null rather than fabricating a number.\n  - New POST /eda endpoint: real pandas/numpy computation of per-column\n    stats (mean/median/std/skew), IQR-based outlier detection with sample\n    rows, Pearson correlation matrix, missing-value report, and categorical\n    top-value frequencies.\n\n- server.ts:\n  - /api/run-ml-prediction now omits `models` for \"auto\" so the Python\n    service''s 5-model default is the single source of truth, and passes\n    through the real `selectionReason` and `shapImportance` fields.\n  - New /api/eda proxy: calls the real EDA computation first, then invokes\n    Gemini strictly to narrate those numbers — same rule as Phase 0, the\n    response schema has no numeric fields, so Gemini cannot report a\n    statistic it didn''t actually compute. Falls back to a template\n    narrative built from the same real numbers when no API key is set.\n\n- src/components/MLPipeline.tsx: the champion banner now shows the real,\n  specific selectionReason instead of a generic message; the comparison\n  table shows every candidate model with both test score and CV mean±std\n  (not just the winner); the feature-importance chart prefers real SHAP\n  values when available, clearly labeled, falling back to the model''s\n  built-in importance otherwise.\n\n- src/components/EDAReport.tsx: new \"Deep EDA (Real, Server-Side)\" tab that\n  calls /api/eda on demand and shows the real skew/outlier/correlation/\n  missing-value numbers plus the narrative, data quality flags, and\n  recommended next steps.\n\n- src/types.ts: added EdaReport type and extended MLResult with\n  selectionReason/shapImportance.\n\nVerified with a full local integration run through the real Node+Python\nstack: 5-model AutoML naturally produced a real tie-break case (Logistic\nRegression vs Random Forest, near-identical CV means resolved by lower\nvariance) exactly as specified, SHAP explained all 5 model families\ncorrectly (including the MLP predict_proba fix) for both classification\nand regression, and /eda returned genuine stats end-to-end.","tree":{"sha":"07512d7d9ca751941b25ba853c7c5b8e930fe90c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/trees/07512d7d9ca751941b25ba853c7c5b8e930fe90c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/commits/2268eddc46e9f521a4f1eb9676f4c04aa79df6db","verification":{"payload":"tree 07512d7d9ca751941b25ba853c7c5b8e930fe90c\nparent 2f616cf3358dcc55288d8f50afd080643ad33e65\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785181292 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785181292 +0000\n\nPhase 1: real AutoML core — multi-model, explainable, real EDA\n\nExtends Phase 0''s real training into an actual AutoML pipeline: multiple\ngenuine candidates compared honestly (losers included), an explainable\nselection rule instead of a black box, real SHAP explainability, and a\nreal server-side EDA endpoint.\n\n- mlops_service/main.py:\n  - AutoML now trains 5 real candidates by default (added\n    GradientBoostingClassifier/Regressor alongside the existing\n    Linear/Logistic, RandomForest, XGBoost, MLP).\n  - Champion selection changed from ranking by a single test-set score to\n    ranking by mean cross-validation score, tie-broken by lower fold-to-fold\n    variance — the exact rule is returned as `selectionReason`, a plain-\n    language string built from the real numbers, not hidden in the backend.\n  - Added real SHAP explainability for the champion model: TreeExplainer for\n    tree-based models, LinearExplainer for linear/logistic, and a bounded\n    generic Explainer for MLP (fixed a real bug where the MLP path passed\n    `.predict` — which returns string class labels — into SHAP''s numeric\n    masking code; classification now correctly explains `.predict_proba`).\n    Values are aggregated back to original column names and returned as\n    `shapImportance`, capped to the top 10 features; failures degrade to\n    null rather than fabricating a number.\n  - New POST /eda endpoint: real pandas/numpy computation of per-column\n    stats (mean/median/std/skew), IQR-based outlier detection with sample\n    rows, Pearson correlation matrix, missing-value report, and categorical\n    top-value frequencies.\n\n- server.ts:\n  - /api/run-ml-prediction now omits `models` for \"auto\" so the Python\n    service''s 5-model default is the single source of truth, and passes\n    through the real `selectionReason` and `shapImportance` fields.\n  - New /api/eda proxy: calls the real EDA computation first, then invokes\n    Gemini strictly to narrate those numbers — same rule as Phase 0, the\n    response schema has no numeric fields, so Gemini cannot report a\n    statistic it didn''t actually compute. Falls back to a template\n    narrative built from the same real numbers when no API key is set.\n\n- src/components/MLPipeline.tsx: the champion banner now shows the real,\n  specific selectionReason instead of a generic message; the comparison\n  table shows every candidate model with both test score and CV mean±std\n  (not just the winner); the feature-importance chart prefers real SHAP\n  values when available, clearly labeled, falling back to the model''s\n  built-in importance otherwise.\n\n- src/components/EDAReport.tsx: new \"Deep EDA (Real, Server-Side)\" tab that\n  calls /api/eda on demand and shows the real skew/outlier/correlation/\n  missing-value numbers plus the narrative, data quality flags, and\n  recommended next steps.\n\n- src/types.ts: added EdaReport type and extended MLResult with\n  selectionReason/shapImportance.\n\nVerified with a full local integration run through the real Node+Python\nstack: 5-model AutoML naturally produced a real tie-break case (Logistic\nRegression vs Random Forest, near-identical CV means resolved by lower\nvariance) exactly as specified, SHAP explained all 5 model families\ncorrectly (including the MLP predict_proba fix) for both classification\nand regression, and /eda returned genuine stats end-to-end.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJt1H+xM\nAx7mk4mUV7KFOtQ09IHskSCpnLGZVdF55aZwIlOWGWh1iITlNJcr2BGJTOS5bdPcpNmf3iuUaxXv\n2A4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T07:29:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https:/