bd6604cec2bbb2f3d542a8db48d92e04509","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/edbcebd6604cec2bbb2f3d542a8db48d92e04509"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commit/2f616cf3358dcc55288d8f50afd080643ad33e65","sha":"2f616cf3358dcc55288d8f50afd080643ad33e65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/2f616cf3358dcc55288d8f50afd080643ad33e65"}],"sha":"0d850ee334e16ba55fdb1c52cf4e0d6e29d9ef0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/0d850ee334e16ba55fdb1c52cf4e0d6e29d9ef0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/commits/2f616cf3358dcc55288d8f50afd080643ad33e65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:02:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:02:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 0: replace fake AutoML with real computation\n\nThe AutoML Pipeline previously fabricated every metric it showed: Gemini was\nprompted to invent \"realistic\" accuracy/R2/F1/etc. numbers, and a large\nclient-side JS function generated fake confusion matrices, fake ensemble\ntrees, and a fake neural network (random weight matrices, formulaic loss\ncurves) — none of it backed by a trained model. A separate \"MLOps\" dashboard\nclaimed to run \"Native Python Compute\" but actually hit hardcoded Express\nmocks, ignoring the real (but unused) FastAPI service that already existed.\n\nThis replaces all of that with genuine training end to end:\n\n- mlops_service/main.py: rebuilt into a real training service. Proper\n  sklearn Pipeline (imputation + scaling + one-hot encoding) fit only on the\n  train split, real train/test split, real 5-fold cross-validation, and\n  actual LinearRegression/LogisticRegression, RandomForest, XGBoost, and MLP\n  models. Returns real R2/MSE/RMSE/MAE or Accuracy/Precision/Recall/F1/\n  ROC-AUC/confusion matrix, real feature importances mapped back to original\n  columns, real RandomForest tree splits, real OOB score, and a real MLP\n  loss/validation curve. Fixed several real bugs along the way: XGBoost\n  rejecting string labels, sklearn''s clone() requiring BaseEstimator\n  compliance, pos_label handling for non-{0,1} binary targets, and the\n  original single-file joblib/predict-encoding mismatch. Models are now\n  stored per-request by id so concurrent users don''t clobber each other''s\n  artifact.\n\n- server.ts: /api/run-ml-prediction now trains via the Python service first,\n  then calls Gemini strictly to narrate the real numbers — its response\n  schema has no numeric metric fields, so it cannot return a fabricated\n  accuracy/F1/etc, and a system prompt forbids inventing any figure not\n  present in the real metrics it''s given. When no API key is configured, a\n  template narrative is built from the same real numbers instead of the old\n  hardcoded 0.894/0.868 constants. The mock /api/train, /api/predict,\n  /api/drift-metrics handlers are now real proxies to the Python service,\n  and a new /api/ml/download proxies the real joblib artifact. If the\n  compute service is unreachable, callers get a clear 503 instead of a\n  silently fabricated \"success\".\n\n- src/utils/mlEngine.ts: removed the fabricator (executeMLOrchestrator) and\n  its random-noise metrics/estimators/deep-learning/comparison generation.\n  Kept the parts that were already real (leakage audit, K-Means, PCA, target\n  suitability) and added genuine silhouette/Davies-Bouldin computation to\n  replace the `0.52 + Math.random() * 0.15` placeholders.\n\n- src/components/MLPipeline.tsx: results now render from the real training\n  response instead of the local fabricator. Algorithm selector trimmed to\n  what''s actually trainable; Ensemble/Deep Learning tabs show an honest\n  empty state instead of fake data when the champion model doesn''t produce\n  that kind of output; model download now streams the real .joblib file;\n  training log copy reflects a real, slower network call.\n\n- src/components/MLOpsDashboard.tsx: \"1-Click Deploy\" trains a real model on\n  the active dataset; drift monitoring runs a real KS-test comparing two\n  real halves of the dataset (labeled honestly, since there''s no live\n  production stream to compare against).\n\n- src/App.tsx: sends the full dataset to the server (not a 30-row sample),\n  and removed getClientSideMLFallback, which used to fabricate metrics\n  client-side whenever the network call looked like it failed.\n\n- src/components/StakeholderDashboard.tsx: the ROC-AUC badge no longer\n  derives a fake number from accuracy*1.05; it shows the real rocAuc from\n  the trained model, or \"N/A\" when not available.\n\nVerified with a full local integration run (Python service + Node server\nwired together): real training across binary/multiclass/regression,\nmulti-model comparison, cross-validation, tree/loss-curve extraction, drift\ndetection, model download, and — critically — a genuine 503 with an\nactionable message when the compute service is stopped, instead of a\nfabricated result.","tree":{"sha":"00a395a9e662c08a41cd64266229f9e7c82d846e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/trees/00a395a9e662c08a41cd64266229f9e7c82d846e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thedeepakreddy/DataScienceStudio-AskDeepakAI/git/commits/2f616cf3358dcc55288d8f50afd080643ad33e65","verification":{"payload":"tree 00a395a9e662c08a41cd64266229f9e7c82d846e\nparent edbcebd6604cec2bbb2f3d542a8db48d92e04509\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785178977 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785178977 +0000\n\nPhase 0: replace fake AutoML with real computation\n\nThe AutoML Pipeline previously fabricated every metric it showed: Gemini was\nprompted to invent \"realistic\" accuracy/R2/F1/etc. numbers, and a large\nclient-side JS function generated fake confusion matrices, fake ensemble\ntrees, and a fake neural network (random weight matrices, formulaic loss\ncurves) — none of it backed by a trained model. A separate \"MLOps\" dashboard\nclaimed to run \"Native Python Compute\" but actually hit hardcoded Express\nmocks, ignoring the real (but unused) FastAPI service that already existed.\n\nThis replaces all of that with genuine training end to end:\n\n- mlops_service/main.py: rebuilt into a real training service. Proper\n  sklearn Pipeline (imputation + scaling + one-hot encoding) fit only on the\n  train split, real train/test split, real 5-fold cross-validation, and\n  actual LinearRegression/LogisticRegression, RandomForest, XGBoost, and MLP\n  models. Returns real R2/MSE/RMSE/MAE or Accuracy/Precision/Recall/F1/\n  ROC-AUC/confusion matrix, real feature importances mapped back to original\n  columns, real RandomForest tree splits, real OOB score, and a real MLP\n  loss/validation curve. Fixed several real bugs along the way: XGBoost\n  rejecting string labels, sklearn''s clone() requiring BaseEstimator\n  compliance, pos_label handling for non-{0,1} binary targets, and the\n  original single-file joblib/predict-encoding mismatch. Models are now\n  stored per-request by id so concurrent users don''t clobber each other''s\n  artifact.\n\n- server.ts: /api/run-ml-prediction now trains via the Python service first,\n  then calls Gemini strictly to narrate the real numbers — its response\n  schema has no numeric metric fields, so it cannot return a fabricated\n  accuracy/F1/etc, and a system prompt forbids inventing any figure not\n  present in the real metrics it''s given. When no API key is configured, a\n  template narrative is built from the same real numbers instead of the old\n  hardcoded 0.894/0.868 constants. The mock /api/train, /api/predict,\n  /api/drift-metrics handlers are now real proxies to the Python service,\n  and a new /api/ml/download proxies the real joblib artifact. If the\n  compute service is unreachable, callers get a clear 503 instead of a\n  silently fabricated \"success\".\n\n- src/utils/mlEngine.ts: removed the fabricator (executeMLOrchestrator) and\n  its random-noise metrics/estimators/deep-learning/comparison generation.\n  Kept the parts that were already real (leakage audit, K-Means, PCA, target\n  suitability) and added genuine silhouette/Davies-Bouldin computation to\n  replace the `0.52 + Math.random() * 0.15` placeholders.\n\n- src/components/MLPipeline.tsx: results now render from the real training\n  response instead of the local fabricator. Algorithm selector trimmed to\n  what''s actually trainable; Ensemble/Deep Learning tabs show an honest\n  empty state instead of fake data when the champion model doesn''t produce\n  that kind of output; model download now streams the real .joblib file;\n  training log copy reflects a real, slower network call.\n\n- src/components/MLOpsDashboard.tsx: \"1-Click Deploy\" trains a real model on\n  the active dataset; drift monitoring runs a real KS-test comparing two\n  real halves of the dataset (labeled honestly, since there''s no live\n  production stream to compare against).\n\n- src/App.tsx: sends the full dataset to the server (not a 30-row sample),\n  and removed getClientSideMLFallback, which used to fabricate metrics\n  client-side whenever the network call looked like it failed.\n\n- src/components/StakeholderDashboard.tsx: the ROC-AUC badge no longer\n  derives a fake number from accuracy*1.05; it shows the real rocAuc from\n  the trained model, or \"N/A\" when not available.\n\nVerified with a full local integration run (Python service + Node server\nwired together): real training across binary/multiclass/regression,\nmulti-model comparison, cross-validation, tree/loss-curve extraction, drift\ndetection, model download, and — critically — a genuine 503 with an\nactionable message when the compute service is stopped, instead of a\nfabricated result.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGxfu39V\nH9/fcPY1BFTtfhnbj9ANaez42RcX8aGNRQQONOG2WtIWqNq7ZOOVxEPb4SJISq9lMKlb3G+QYYos\njwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T19:23:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"h