/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/831439060fa1f7c5b10a201c013666fd8ac404fe","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKDgzMTQzOTA2MGZhMWY3YzViMTBhMjAxYzAxMzY2NmZkOGFjNDA0ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/46cf3101a0c7b2d420e3df5f0e409afa270df16e","sha":"46cf3101a0c7b2d420e3df5f0e409afa270df16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/46cf3101a0c7b2d420e3df5f0e409afa270df16e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/9708214a79fa2ffa2911b9eba5ed8cd2e8ae1c5f","sha":"9708214a79fa2ffa2911b9eba5ed8cd2e8ae1c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/9708214a79fa2ffa2911b9eba5ed8cd2e8ae1c5f"}],"sha":"831439060fa1f7c5b10a201c013666fd8ac404fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/831439060fa1f7c5b10a201c013666fd8ac404fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/9708214a79fa2ffa2911b9eba5ed8cd2e8ae1c5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T16:43:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T16:43:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"examples/blog-go: hello-blog tutorial — sqlite + raw SQL + sessions\n\nThe full hello-blog from FULLSTACK.md''s tutorial decision. Exercises\nall three Go packages end-to-end against a real sqlite database,\nwith stdlib net/http for routing and raw database/sql for queries —\nevery concrete choice (sqlite vs Postgres, stdlib vs chi, raw SQL\nvs sqlc) is independent of Salmo, which only owns what''s under\nserver/.\n\nWhat it does:\n- GET  /            list posts + \"you''ve posted N times\" counter\n- GET  /new         post-form\n- POST /posts       insert post, redirect to /posts/{id}\n- GET  /posts/{id}  show one post\n\nDemonstrates:\n- dsd.Component implementations using html/template for auto-escaped\n  interpolation (HomePage, PostDetail, PostForm)\n- session.CookieStore[Identity] for anonymous-but-stable visitor IDs\n  via the session.identityOrIssue pattern (read; issue + Set-Cookie\n  if absent/invalid)\n- render.Page wrapping each route''s component in the HTML scaffold\n- Raw SQL through database/sql against modernc.org/sqlite (pure Go,\n  no CGO) — the first external Go dep in the repo, scoped to this\n  example''s own go.mod\n\nWhat it does NOT load:\n- No Salmo JS runtime. The blog is pure server-rendered HTML; the\n  only interactivity is browser-native form submission. See\n  examples/server-hello/ for the JS hydration flow.\n\nCaveats documented in README:\n- The session-signing secret regenerates on each run (throwaway\n  demo behaviour; production loads from env/vault)\n- No CSRF protection (out of scope for the tutorial)\n- html/template handles XSS for dynamic values automatically\n\nSmoke-tested end-to-end via curl:\n- GET / on empty DB shows \"No posts yet. Be the first.\"\n- POST /posts → 303 redirect to /posts/1 showing the new post\n- GET / now shows \"You''ve posted 1 time\" (singular/plural aware)\n  and the post appears in the list\n\nLayout: everything in main.go (~280 LOC) on purpose so the tutorial\nreads in one sitting. The example has its own go.mod with replace\ngithub.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/server => ../../server, matching the\npattern from examples/server-hello.\n\nFULLSTACK.md and README.md status tables updated.","tree":{"sha":"53c583a989781351b38b3a22bfe2be8330a30e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/53c583a989781351b38b3a22bfe2be8330a30e05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/9708214a79fa2ffa2911b9eba5ed8cd2e8ae1c5f","verification":{"payload":"tree 53c583a989781351b38b3a22bfe2be8330a30e05\nparent 46cf3101a0c7b2d420e3df5f0e409afa270df16e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780418608 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780418608 +0000\n\nexamples/blog-go: hello-blog tutorial — sqlite + raw SQL + sessions\n\nThe full hello-blog from FULLSTACK.md''s tutorial decision. Exercises\nall three Go packages end-to-end against a real sqlite database,\nwith stdlib net/http for routing and raw database/sql for queries —\nevery concrete choice (sqlite vs Postgres, stdlib vs chi, raw SQL\nvs sqlc) is independent of Salmo, which only owns what''s under\nserver/.\n\nWhat it does:\n- GET  /            list posts + \"you''ve posted N times\" counter\n- GET  /new         post-form\n- POST /posts       insert post, redirect to /posts/{id}\n- GET  /posts/{id}  show one post\n\nDemonstrates:\n- dsd.Component implementations using html/template for auto-escaped\n  interpolation (HomePage, PostDetail, PostForm)\n- session.CookieStore[Identity] for anonymous-but-stable visitor IDs\n  via the session.identityOrIssue pattern (read; issue + Set-Cookie\n  if absent/invalid)\n- render.Page wrapping each route''s component in the HTML scaffold\n- Raw SQL through database/sql against modernc.org/sqlite (pure Go,\n  no CGO) — the first external Go dep in the repo, scoped to this\n  example''s own go.mod\n\nWhat it does NOT load:\n- No Salmo JS runtime. The blog is pure server-rendered HTML; the\n  only interactivity is browser-native form submission. See\n  examples/server-hello/ for the JS hydration flow.\n\nCaveats documented in README:\n- The session-signing secret regenerates on each run (throwaway\n  demo behaviour; production loads from env/vault)\n- No CSRF protection (out of scope for the tutorial)\n- html/template handles XSS for dynamic values automatically\n\nSmoke-tested end-to-end via curl:\n- GET / on empty DB shows \"No posts yet. Be the first.\"\n- POST /posts → 303 redirect to /posts/1 showing the new post\n- GET / now shows \"You''ve posted 1 time\" (singular/plural aware)\n  and the post appears in the list\n\nLayout: everything in main.go (~280 LOC) on purpose so the tutorial\nreads in one sitting. The example has its own go.mod with replace\ngithub.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/server => ../../server, matching the\npattern from examples/server-hello.\n\nFULLSTACK.md and README.md status tables updated.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfF