he previous commit included the compiled server-hello binary\nfrom a local smoke test. Removing and adding .gitignore so\nfuture `go build .` runs don''t repeat this.","tree":{"sha":"bf1d5cb49e19b250c7335bb077b8044b6cb30b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/bf1d5cb49e19b250c7335bb077b8044b6cb30b65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/fcebf64178b4feb48d5fa245e7cd8ec779532df3","verification":{"payload":"tree bf1d5cb49e19b250c7335bb077b8044b6cb30b65\nparent db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780251725 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780251725 +0000\n\nexamples/server-hello: drop accidentally-committed binary, add .gitignore\n\nThe previous commit included the compiled server-hello binary\nfrom a local smoke test. Removing and adding .gitignore so\nfuture `go build .` runs don''t repeat this.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHb5gdnZ\nKg0Q1akK3yQsSE6dnSU5q72XSAMtnGQNeSt8KQ0na5QFvuJUpG5IuADmhoj5dqQCWLlFthf0+ZnV\nEgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-31T18:22:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fcebf64178b4feb48d5fa245e7cd8ec779532df3","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGZjZWJmNjQxNzhiNGZlYjQ4ZDVmYTI0NWU3Y2Q4ZWM3Nzk1MzJkZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859","sha":"db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859"}],"sha":"fcebf64178b4feb48d5fa245e7cd8ec779532df3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fcebf64178b4feb48d5fa245e7cd8ec779532df3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T18:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T18:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"merge-readiness: parity tests, e2e example, README cross-links\n\nCloses the four gaps flagged before merging this branch into main:\n\n1. Working end-to-end example: examples/server-hello/\n2. Wire-format parity test: server/dsd/parity_test.go + regen script\n3. Root README mention of the Go server\n4. (Branch base — handled separately in the PR/merge step)\n\nWire-format parity (gap #2):\n\nProbing Node SSR exposed two real discrepancies between this Go\nrenderer and the reference implementation, both now fixed in\nthe Go renderer to match Node:\n\n- Attribute escape rules. Per WHATWG HTML serialization for\n  double-quoted attribute values, only & and \" require escaping;\n  <, >, and '' stay raw. The Go renderer was over-escaping all\n  five (and using &#34; instead of &quot;). Now matches Node\n  byte-for-byte after comment stripping.\n\n- SSR.md rule (4) was incorrect about which characters need\n  escaping. Now states the text-content escape set (&, <, >) and\n  the attribute-value escape set (&, \") separately, and explains\n  the Go renderer''s split of responsibilities (it does attribute\n  escaping, pushes text-content escaping to the component''s\n  template.HTML output).\n\nNew \"Cross-implementation parity\" section in SSR.md defines\nsemantic equivalence precisely: same DOM tree after browser parse,\nignoring HTML comments (lit-html emits <!----> markers; Go does\nnot — both spec-valid). Implementations differ on whitespace,\nattribute order (Go sorts for byte-stability; Node doesn''t), and\nescape-canonical choices among spec-valid options.\n\nserver/dsd/parity_test.go pins four cases (light DOM, shadow DOM,\nattribute & + < raw, attribute \" escape) against expected\nstrings captured from Node. server/dsd/testdata/regen-parity.mjs\nre-runs the Node side and prints the strings to diff against\nthe test constants — documented for use whenever the renderer\nchanges or lit-html/happy-dom updates.\n\nEnd-to-end example (gap #1):\n\nexamples/server-hello/ is a 100-line Go server (own go.mod with\nreplace pointing at ../../server) that:\n\n- Defines a Greeting component satisfying dsd.Component +\n  Shadower + Attributer\n- Renders it via render.Page with the Salmo CDN runtime URL +\n  a client-side app.js\n- Embeds static/ via //go:embed so the binary is self-contained\n- Verified end-to-end with a curl smoke test: DSD scaffold\n  emits correctly, x-greeting host wraps the shadow template,\n  /static/app.js returns 200\n\nThe client app.js redefines x-greeting with a reactive counter,\nso the visible browser story is: server-rendered greeting\npaints instantly (from DSD), JS loads, button appears once the\nclient component upgrades the host. README in the example\nexplains what to look for and what the example deliberately\ndoes NOT demonstrate (v0.2.0 true hydration, federation,\nsessions — those land in blog-go later).\n\nRoot README (gap #3):\n\nNew \"Server-side rendering with Go\" section between Quickstart\nand Examples, with a tight code snippet, links to the three\nserver packages, and a pointer to FULLSTACK.md for the design\nrationale. server-hello added to the Examples table.\n\nFULLSTACK.md \"What''s landed\" table updated with parity test\nand example rows.\n\nTests: 84 JS unit + 70 conformance + 45 Go (18 dsd including 4\nparity + 13 render + 14 session). Clean typecheck.","tree":{"sha":"c5b818ad9dbc56e5a80aeeeb680a504a40dacb5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/c5b818ad9dbc56e5a80aeeeb680a504a40dacb5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859","verification":{"payload":"tree c5b818ad9dbc56e5a80aeeeb680a504a40dacb5a\nparent 4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780251714 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780251714 +0000\n\nmerge-readiness: parity tests, e2e example, README cross-links\n\nCloses the four gaps flagged before merging this branch into main:\n\n1. Working end-to-end example: examples/server-hello/\n2. Wire-format parity test: server/dsd/parity_test.go + regen script\n3. Root README mention of the Go server\n4. (Branch base — handled separately in the PR/merge step)\n\nWire-format parity (gap #2):\n\nProbing Node SSR exposed two real discrepancies between this Go\nrenderer and the reference implementation, both now fixed in\nthe Go renderer to match Node:\n\n- Attribute escape rules. Per WHATWG HTML serialization for\n  double-quoted attribute values, only & and \" require escaping;\n  <, >, and '' stay raw. The Go renderer was over-escaping all\n  five (and using &#34; instead of &quot;). Now matches Node\n  byte-for-byte after comment stripping.\n\n- SSR.md rule (4) was incorrect about which characters need\n  escaping. Now states the text-content escape set (&, <, >) and\n  the attribute-value escape set (&, \") separately, and explains\n  the Go renderer''s split of responsibilities (it does attribute\n  escaping, pushes text-content escaping to the component''s\n  template.HTML output).\n\nNew \"Cross-implementation parity\" section in SSR.md defines\nsemantic equivalence precisely: same DOM tree after browser parse,\nignoring HTML comments (lit-html emits <!----> markers; Go does\nnot — both spec-valid). Implementations differ on whitespace,\nattribute order (Go sorts for byte-stability; Node doesn''t), and\nescape-canonical choices among spec-valid options.\n\nserver/dsd/parity_test.go pins four cases (light DOM, shadow DOM,\nattribute & + < raw, attribute \" escape) against expected\nstrings captured from Node. server/dsd/testdata/regen-parity.mjs\nre-runs the Node side and prints the strings to diff against\nthe test constants — documented for use whenever the renderer\nchanges or lit-html/happy-dom updates.\n\nEnd-to-end example (gap #1):\n\nexamples/server-hello/ is a 100-line Go server (own go.mod with\nreplace pointing at ../../server) that:\n\n- Defines a Greeting component satisfying dsd.Component +\n  Shadower + Attributer\n- Renders it via render.Page with the Salmo CDN runtime URL +\n  a client-side app.js\n- Embeds static/ via //go:embed so the binary is self-contained\n- Verified end-to-end with a curl smoke test: DSD scaffold\n  emits correctly, x-greeting host wraps the shadow template,\n  /static/app.js returns 200\n\nThe client app.js redefines x-greeting with a reactive counter,\nso the visible browser story is: server-rendered greeting\npaints instantly (from DSD), JS loads, button appears once the\nclient component upgrades the host. README in the example\nexplains what to look for and what the example deliberately\ndoes NOT demonstrate (v0.2.0 true hydration, federation,\nsessions — those land in blog-go later).\n\nRoot README (gap #3):\n\nNew \"Server-side rendering with Go\" section between Quickstart\nand Examples, with a tight code snippet, links to the three\nserver packages, and a pointer to FULLSTACK.md for the design\nrationale. server-hello added to the Examples table.\n\nFULLSTACK.md \"What''s landed\" table updated with parity test\nand example rows.\n\nTests: 84 JS unit + 70 conformance + 45 Go (18 dsd including 4\nparity + 13 render + 14 session). Clean typecheck.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG5otF8j\nvSjRiwyuAbLE+VrG5AZDA+hqbFnZqSKpBT+qaQwNZxcqz8vzon4RA8S9HKm2WQqv89qnPzsn2Adx\nvAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-31T18:21:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGRiNDdhZTY3YTRmNzA0NDcxNGJlYjdiZTkwMzNkMjEyNjcyZjg4NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994","sha":"4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994"}],"sha":"db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/db47ae67a4f7044714beb7be9033d212672f8859"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T15:27:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T15:27:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"server/session: Store[T] interface + cookie+HMAC default\n\nThird slice on top of dsd + render. Defines the server-side\nsession contract that the AUTH.md \"framework owns the wiring,\napp owns the policy\" principle predicted, with a default\nimplementation safe to use without an external store.\n\nInterface:\n\n  type Store[T any] interface {\n      Get(r *http.Request) (T, error)\n      Set(w http.ResponseWriter, value T) error\n      Destroy(w http.ResponseWriter) error\n  }\n\nT is the application''s session payload — a user ID, a struct\nwith claims, anything that round-trips through encoding/json.\nGeneric so the type checker enforces payload shape end-to-end\n(no map[string]any). Sentinel errors ErrNoSession and\nErrInvalidSession distinguish \"no session\" from \"tampered or\nexpired session\" from other backend errors.\n\nDefault implementation: CookieStore[T].\n\n- HMAC-SHA256 envelope: base64url(json({v: value, e: expiryUnix}))\n  + \".\" + base64url(HMAC(secret, that))\n- Secret must be >= 32 bytes (NIST SP 800-107 baseline for\n  HMAC-SHA256). Defensively copied so the caller can zero\n  their buffer.\n- Server-side expiry stamp in the envelope is the source of\n  truth; cookie MaxAge is a transport hint to the browser. A\n  server that sees an expired envelope rejects regardless of\n  what the browser sent.\n- DefaultCookieOptions() returns production-safe defaults:\n  HttpOnly=true, Secure=true, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, MaxAge=24h.\n  Name is left empty so apps must namespace explicitly.\n- Constant-time signature comparison via hmac.Equal.\n\nSecurity note documented in the package doc: HMAC provides\nintegrity, not confidentiality. The payload is readable by\nanyone with the cookie. Apps that need confidentiality use an\nopaque server-side ID and back it with a real Store\nimplementation (Redis, Postgres, etc).\n\nWhat''s deliberately out of scope:\n- encryption (caller composes if needed)\n- rotation on read (caller can Set on every request)\n- multi-cookie-key support for key rotation (caller wraps Get\n  to try multiple stores; cheap pattern)\n- a HandlerFunc middleware that injects session into context\n  (premature — different apps want different context shapes)\n\nTests: 14/14 covering constructor validation (short secret,\nempty name, defensive copy), round-trips for both scalar\n(userID) and struct (sessionData) payloads, all error paths\n(no cookie, malformed, tampered payload, tampered signature,\ndifferent secret), expiry (with overridable now() for\ndeterminism), zero-MaxAge \"session cookie\" behaviour, Destroy\nemits a negative-MaxAge cookie, and default security\nattributes (HttpOnly + Secure + SameSiteLax).\n\nModule-wide: 14 (dsd) + 13 (render) + 14 (session) = 41 tests\npassing. Compile-time assertion confirms CookieStore[T]\nsatisfies Store[T].\n\nAUTH.md updated: cross-references server/session/, and the\nownership table gains three rows distinguishing contract\n(framework) from backend (app default + swap-in) from\nvalidation policy (app).","tree":{"sha":"6c19b04f5448ba17d1e9bfbdb5a3ce4bac9c0ce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/6c19b04f5448ba17d1e9bfbdb5a3ce4bac9c0ce7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c19b04f5448ba17d1e9bfbdb5a3ce4bac9c0ce7\nparent 1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780241232 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780241232 +0000\n\nserver/session: Store[T] interface + cookie+HMAC default\n\nThird slice on top of dsd + render. Defines the server-side\nsession contract that the AUTH.md \"framework owns the wiring,\napp owns the policy\" principle predicted, with a default\nimplementation safe to use without an external store.\n\nInterface:\n\n  type Store[T any] interface {\n      Get(r *http.Request) (T, error)\n      Set(w http.ResponseWriter, value T) error\n      Destroy(w http.ResponseWriter) error\n  }\n\nT is the application''s session payload — a user ID, a struct\nwith claims, anything that round-trips through encoding/json.\nGeneric so the type checker enforces payload shape end-to-end\n(no map[string]any). Sentinel errors ErrNoSession and\nErrInvalidSession distinguish \"no session\" from \"tampered or\nexpired session\" from other backend errors.\n\nDefault implementation: CookieStore[T].\n\n- HMAC-SHA256 envelope: base64url(json({v: value, e: expiryUnix}))\n  + \".\" + base64url(HMAC(secret, that))\n- Secret must be >= 32 bytes (NIST SP 800-107 baseline for\n  HMAC-SHA256). Defensively copied so the caller can zero\n  their buffer.\n- Server-side expiry stamp in the envelope is the source of\n  truth; cookie MaxAge is a transport hint to the browser. A\n  server that sees an expired envelope rejects regardless of\n  what the browser sent.\n- DefaultCookieOptions() returns production-safe defaults:\n  HttpOnly=true, Secure=true, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, MaxAge=24h.\n  Name is left empty so apps must namespace explicitly.\n- Constant-time signature comparison via hmac.Equal.\n\nSecurity note documented in the package doc: HMAC provides\nintegrity, not confidentiality. The payload is readable by\nanyone with the cookie. Apps that need confidentiality use an\nopaque server-side ID and back it with a real Store\nimplementation (Redis, Postgres, etc).\n\nWhat''s deliberately out of scope:\n- encryption (caller composes if needed)\n- rotation on read (caller can Set on every request)\n- multi-cookie-key support for key rotation (caller wraps Get\n  to try multiple stores; cheap pattern)\n- a HandlerFunc middleware that injects session into context\n  (premature — different apps want different context shapes)\n\nTests: 14/14 covering constructor validation (short secret,\nempty name, defensive copy), round-trips for both scalar\n(userID) and struct (sessionData) payloads, all error paths\n(no cookie, malformed, tampered payload, tampered signature,\ndifferent secret), expiry (with overridable now() for\ndeterminism), zero-MaxAge \"session cookie\" behaviour, Destroy\nemits a negative-MaxAge cookie, and default security\nattributes (HttpOnly + Secure + SameSiteLax).\n\nModule-wide: 14 (dsd) + 13 (render) + 14 (session) = 41 tests\npassing. Compile-time assertion confirms CookieStore[T]\nsatisfies Store[T].\n\nAUTH.md updated: cross-references server/session/, and the\nownership table gains three rows distinguishing contract\n(framework) from backend (app default + swap-in) from\nvalidation policy (app).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP2FrXh0\naujY/lMsxfwns5NdtevLEFI/3hpTruw0I3sVFxNm1Rrb3un9sId7xU0Nxj8NWlZVwltOiya37xqZ\nhwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-31T15:27:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKDRhNDg5YjFmMzY5NGExZjE2MDIwNDdjN2IyMDE2N2U0ZWQ2OTc5OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4","sha":"1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4"}],"sha":"4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/4a489b1f3694a1f1602047c7b20167e4ed697994"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T15:20:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T15:20:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"server/render: Fragment + Page http.Handler helpers\n\nThe next slice on top of server/dsd: glue that lets a Go HTTP\nhandler turn a Salmo component into a response. Two entry points\ncovering the two real use cases:\n\n- Fragment(w, r, component) writes a single component as the\n  response body. For HTMX-style partial updates and any handler\n  that returns component HTML to be inserted into an existing\n  page.\n\n- Page(w, r, opts, body) writes a full HTML5 document with the\n  component as the sole child of <body>. PageOpts configures\n  <title>, <html lang>, <meta charset>, script-module URLs in\n  <head>, and raw head injection for users who need SRI-bearing\n  <script> tags or arbitrary <meta>/<link>.\n\nBoth buffer the rendered HTML before touching the\nhttp.ResponseWriter. A render error leaves w untouched so the\ncaller can write a custom error response (typically http.Error\nwith the status code their handler wants). Content-Type is set\nto text/html; charset=utf-8 on success.\n\nThe package deliberately does not own:\n- routing (chi, echo, stdlib net/http — bring your own)\n- error response shape (caller decides — they have status code,\n  log fields, observability context)\n- streaming (whole document buffered; per SSR.md, streaming\n  across remotes is out of scope for v1)\n- a HandlerFunc wrapper (premature; Fragment / Page compose into\n  any handler shape in 3 lines)\n\nTests: 13/13 covering happy paths (default scaffold, custom\nlang/charset/title, script ordering, raw head injection, body\ncomponent nesting), escaping (title and lang against\nscript-injection attempts), error paths (render error leaves\nresponse untouched), Content-Type, and one end-to-end test\nagainst a real http.ServeMux + httptest.Server to confirm the\ncanonical usage shape from the godoc actually works.\n\nModule-wide: 14 (dsd) + 13 (render) = 27 tests, all passing.\n\nFULLSTACK.md and server/README.md status tables updated.","tree":{"sha":"927d04a6b4a48ac5bd4287656d6569f3809bb2fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/927d04a6b4a48ac5bd4287656d6569f3809bb2fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 927d04a6b4a48ac5bd4287656d6569f3809bb2fd\nparent 46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780240854 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780240854 +0000\n\nserver/render: Fragment + Page http.Handler helpers\n\nThe next slice on top of server/dsd: glue that lets a Go HTTP\nhandler turn a Salmo component into a response. Two entry points\ncovering the two real use cases:\n\n- Fragment(w, r, component) writes a single component as the\n  response body. For HTMX-style partial updates and any handler\n  that returns component HTML to be inserted into an existing\n  page.\n\n- Page(w, r, opts, body) writes a full HTML5 document with the\n  component as the sole child of <body>. PageOpts configures\n  <title>, <html lang>, <meta charset>, script-module URLs in\n  <head>, and raw head injection for users who need SRI-bearing\n  <script> tags or arbitrary <meta>/<link>.\n\nBoth buffer the rendered HTML before touching the\nhttp.ResponseWriter. A render error leaves w untouched so the\ncaller can write a custom error response (typically http.Error\nwith the status code their handler wants). Content-Type is set\nto text/html; charset=utf-8 on success.\n\nThe package deliberately does not own:\n- routing (chi, echo, stdlib net/http — bring your own)\n- error response shape (caller decides — they have status code,\n  log fields, observability context)\n- streaming (whole document buffered; per SSR.md, streaming\n  across remotes is out of scope for v1)\n- a HandlerFunc wrapper (premature; Fragment / Page compose into\n  any handler shape in 3 lines)\n\nTests: 13/13 covering happy paths (default scaffold, custom\nlang/charset/title, script ordering, raw head injection, body\ncomponent nesting), escaping (title and lang against\nscript-injection attempts), error paths (render error leaves\nresponse untouched), Content-Type, and one end-to-end test\nagainst a real http.ServeMux + httptest.Server to confirm the\ncanonical usage shape from the godoc actually works.\n\nModule-wide: 14 (dsd) + 13 (render) = 27 tests, all passing.\n\nFULLSTACK.md and server/README.md status tables updated.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK+vP3SZ\n6Csqu3eElyw9u0ZaCEHpdHhIOCo+tEvReuGevdWwjXmyfQFME8FRMt+Z6YeWt3tslydi2WlVlBhb\nzwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-31T15:20:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKDEzNDBiNDM0ZWVjMWNiM2NlN2YyNjE5YjBiMmVmMzlhNjYyODg3YzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6","sha":"46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6"}],"sha":"1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/1340b434eec1cb3ce7f2619b0b2ef39a662887c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T15:11:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T15:11:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"server/dsd: Go renderer for SSR.md protocol rules (1)-(4)\n\nFirst concrete Go-side deliverable for the fullstack story in\nFULLSTACK.md. server/dsd/ implements the DSD wire format as a\nstandalone Go package — Salmo''s Node renderer in src/ssr.js is\nthe reference implementation; this is the second.\n\nSurface:\n- Component interface (Tag + Render → template.HTML)\n- Shadower optional interface (protocol rule 2: <template\n  shadowrootmode=\"open\"> wrapper)\n- Attributer optional interface (rules 1 + 4: attributes with\n  HTML-escaped values, sorted lexicographically for byte-stable\n  output across runs)\n- Render(ctx, c) entrypoint, returns template.HTML or error\n\nWhat this validates:\n- The SSR.md spec is genuinely language-portable — building a\n  full implementation in Go required no changes to the protocol,\n  no callbacks into JS, no shared runtime\n- The escape set is small enough to freeze (five HTML5 specials,\n  matching template.HTMLEscapeString) — canonical-byte parity\n  with the Node renderer is achievable in a later commit\n- Deterministic attribute ordering matters and is cheap (sort\n  the keys once per component)\n\nTests: 14/14 covering both happy paths (light DOM, shadow DOM,\nattribute escaping, empty content) and error paths (nil component,\ninvalid tag, invalid attr name, propagated component errors).\n\nModule rooted at server/ so the repo stays JS-only at the top\nlevel. Import path: github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/server/dsd.\n\nFULLSTACK.md updated:\n- \"Open questions\" section now records the four initial decisions\n  with one-line rationale each (explicit interface for salmo.Render,\n  short-lived JWT exchange for cross-origin auth, defer streaming\n  SSR, sqlite+stdlib+raw SQL for the tutorial)\n- New \"What''s landed\" table tracking server/dsd as v0 and the\n  planned follow-ups (render/, session/, federation/, examples/\n  blog-go/)","tree":{"sha":"8ce133d6dd97ffb8a761e5bd28df14fae59aed6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/8ce133d6dd97ffb8a761e5bd28df14fae59aed6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ce133d6dd97ffb8a761e5bd28df14fae59aed6a\nparent fc90cdc0a431db8ce3263ec7d1b077c493fe87e3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780240291 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780240291 +0000\n\nserver/dsd: Go renderer for SSR.md protocol rules (1)-(4)\n\nFirst concrete Go-side deliverable for the fullstack story in\nFULLSTACK.md. server/dsd/ implements the DSD wire format as a\nstandalone Go package — Salmo''s Node renderer in src/ssr.js is\nthe reference implementation; this is the second.\n\nSurface:\n- Component interface (Tag + Render → template.HTML)\n- Shadower optional interface (protocol rule 2: <template\n  shadowrootmode=\"open\"> wrapper)\n- Attributer optional interface (rules 1 + 4: attributes with\n  HTML-escaped values, sorted lexicographically for byte-stable\n  output across runs)\n- Render(ctx, c) entrypoint, returns template.HTML or error\n\nWhat this validates:\n- The SSR.md spec is genuinely language-portable — building a\n  full implementation in Go required no changes to the protocol,\n  no callbacks into JS, no shared runtime\n- The escape set is small enough to freeze (five HTML5 specials,\n  matching template.HTMLEscapeString) — canonical-byte parity\n  with the Node renderer is achievable in a later commit\n- Deterministic attribute ordering matters and is cheap (sort\n  the keys once per component)\n\nTests: 14/14 covering both happy paths (light DOM, shadow DOM,\nattribute escaping, empty content) and error paths (nil component,\ninvalid tag, invalid attr name, propagated component errors).\n\nModule rooted at server/ so the repo stays JS-only at the top\nlevel. Import path: github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/server/dsd.\n\nFULLSTACK.md updated:\n- \"Open questions\" section now records the four initial decisions\n  with one-line rationale each (explicit interface for salmo.Render,\n  short-lived JWT exchange for cross-origin auth, defer streaming\n  SSR, sqlite+stdlib+raw SQL for the tutorial)\n- New \"What''s landed\" table tracking server/dsd as v0 and the\n  planned follow-ups (render/, session/, federation/, examples/\n  blog-go/)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKxMxXsL\n4gBceuT9c2I/iZNOmJku71UlVj08RRnEtvsHSQVi0TeHBJ5O1UpfzZu86R7MxeKnwex6Ab/QXcla\nfQk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-31T15:11:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKDQ2ZGVmZWY2NmZjM2QzOTRjMDgxODAzYTg2OGUzMWNmNjZjNjllYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fc90cdc0a431db8ce3263ec7d1b077c493fe87e3","sha":"fc90cdc0a431db8ce3263ec7d1b077c493fe87e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fc90cdc0a431db8ce3263ec7d1b077c493fe87e3"}],"sha":"46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/46defef66fc3d394c081803a868e31cf66c69ec6"},{"au