m/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fbc368b9839de66e96393989ed0a1f172e5c4d42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T19:34:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T19:34:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"framework: prepare for standalone-repo release\n\nMake framework/ self-contained so it can be extracted as its own\nGitHub repo. Move examples/ → framework/examples/, add the standard\ntop-level files (README, LICENSE, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING), and add\nthree AI-discoverability docs (llms.txt, API.md, COOKBOOK.md).\n\nPath portability: example lazyComponent srcs and the router''s BASE\nare now derived from import.meta.url, so the same demos work whether\nthe framework is mounted at /framework/ (integrated site) or / (its\nown repo root). The notes server''s static-passthrough route handles\nboth prefixes too.\n\npackage.json: 0.0.1 → 0.1.0 with MIT license + repo metadata.\n\nVerified: 80/80 unit tests, 70/70 TC39 Signals conformance,\ntypecheck clean, all 10 demos render with zero JS/network errors\nunder both mount conventions (chromium via playwright).","tree":{"sha":"1a65c4f45ebfb9cee7e3e8928dc462c45bb41b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/1a65c4f45ebfb9cee7e3e8928dc462c45bb41b0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/fbc368b9839de66e96393989ed0a1f172e5c4d42","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fbc368b9839de66e96393989ed0a1f172e5c4d42","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGZiYzM2OGI5ODM5ZGU2NmU5NjM5Mzk4OWVkMGExZjE3MmU1YzRkNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38","sha":"dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38"}],"sha":"fbc368b9839de66e96393989ed0a1f172e5c4d42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fbc368b9839de66e96393989ed0a1f172e5c4d42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T19:13:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T19:13:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"state: framework/STATE.md — four patterns, no new API\n\nSame framing as AUTH.md: provide the primitive, document the\npatterns, don''t ship the library.\n\nPatterns in order of escalation:\n  1. Module-level signal (start here; the catalog is the file)\n  2. Atom registry (#1 conventionalised when signals sprawl)\n  3. Store object factory (Pinia/small-Redux shape; encapsulates\n     mutations so callers don''t put the store in invalid states)\n  4. Context provider (<x-*-provider>; for multiple instances or\n     subtree-scoped state — same pattern as auth-provider)\n\nThe choosing table maps \"you have X\" → \"use Y\" so the decision isn''t\nabstract.\n\nFederation interop section is the bit that''s genuinely interesting:\nbecause the framework is singleton-pinned via the import map, a\nmodule-level signal IS the same instance across host and remote\nbundles. No Redux/Zustand/Pinia/Jotai gives you that for free — they\nall need extra dedup wiring across bundle boundaries. Comparison\ntable at the bottom makes the trade explicit (no batteries, but the\nprimitive composes and federation is free).\n\nDeliberately not shipped: createStore() / createAtom() helpers,\ndispatch(action) reducer protocol, devtools time-travel, middleware,\nhook-style consumer APIs. All app-shaped, none belong in framework/src/.\n\nNo code changes. No new tests. The patterns rest on the existing\nSignal primitive that''s already 70/70 conformant.","tree":{"sha":"35b9eaa59500f88f400a58b8f4e6141241765c9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/35b9eaa59500f88f400a58b8f4e6141241765c9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGRjMzA0N2U2MzdkNzEzNzczMzE5ZmZjMzRjMzY1Njk1MGJhODZhMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc","sha":"e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc"}],"sha":"dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/dc3047e637d713773319ffc34c3656950ba86a38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T19:09:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T19:09:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"auth: framework/AUTH.md + <x-auth-provider> reference example\n\nFrames the framework/application split honestly:\n  Framework owns: Signal primitive, context-via-closest pattern,\n                  federation security (SRI + allowedOrigins).\n  Application owns: cookie vs token choice, refresh strategy,\n                    storage, OAuth flows, login UI.\n\nframework/AUTH.md:\n  Three patterns with worked examples and when to use each:\n   A. HttpOnly cookie → zero plumbing (the browser does it; what the\n      notes app uses; pick this when you can)\n   B. <x-auth-provider> context provider for token auth → host hangs\n      session signal + fetchAuthed on instance state, children read\n      via closest()\n   C. window-global → prototypes only\n  Role-gates section: just when() + signals, no new primitive.\n  Trust-boundary section restated: federated remotes run in your\n  origin; token sharing is ergonomics, not isolation.\n\nexamples/auth-provider/ (reference component, ~120 lines):\n  - <x-auth-provider>: hosts session signal, login/logout/fetchAuthed\n    on instance state. Mock /demo-api/me handler so the demo runs\n    without a backend.\n  - <x-login-panel>: same-bundle consumer demonstrating closest().\n  - <x-private-info> in widgets/private-info.js: federated consumer\n    loaded via lazyComponent. Walks up to the provider, subscribes to\n    the session signal, calls fetchAuthed for an authed request.\n    Auth-related state stays in the host; widget is stateless.\n  Verified in chromium: login → federated widget unlocks → click\n  Fetch button → GET /demo-api/me with Authorization: Bearer …\n  returns 200 with the right user. Logout reverts cleanly. Zero\n  console errors.\n\nFEDERATION.md update:\n  Adds a ''Sharing state with remotes'' section enumerating the three\n  patterns (prop, context provider, module-level singleton) and\n  pointing at AUTH.md / examples/auth-provider/ for the long form.\n\nframework/src/ is unchanged. No new public API. Auth-specific code\nthat doesn''t belong in the framework stays out of the framework.","tree":{"sha":"f6b343b67744447251aa87c7ef4edce6f8fb4bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/f6b343b67744447251aa87c7ef4edce6f8fb4bbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGUzZDUyOWZiMzViNjc5YjQ3YjRkZTgyODFkMDAyMThhNWE5MGFiZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced","sha":"4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced"}],"sha":"e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/e3d529fb35b679b47b4de8281d00218a5a90abfc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T18:44:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T18:44:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"examples/notes — fullstack demo (auth + SSR + federation + persistence)\n\nA real multi-user notes app that exercises every framework feature in\none place. Backend in 290 lines, frontend in 210, plus a 90-line\nplaywright e2e fixture.\n\nBackend (server.mjs):\n  - node:sqlite (built-in, no deps) for storage\n  - node:http for routing\n  - HMAC-signed HttpOnly cookies for sessions (no JWT lib, no session\n    store) — userId.hmac(userId) with timing-safe verify\n  - pbkdf2Sync (100k iterations) for password hashing\n  - setupDOM + renderToString from the framework for SSR\n\nFrontend (app.js):\n  - <x-notes-app> root reads server-rendered `initial` state from a\n    prop, routes between <x-auth> and <x-notes-board>\n  - <x-auth> handles login + signup with one form (mode toggle)\n  - <x-notes-board> owns the list + selectedId + the save/create/\n    remove actions; renders the federated editor\n  - <x-rich-editor> (in widgets/editor.js) is a separate bundle path,\n    loaded via lazyComponent; uses shadow DOM with scoped <style>,\n    emits debounced `change` events\n\nSSR + federation fix on the framework side:\n  - setupDOM() now sets globalThis.__mohsal_ssr__ so lazyComponent\n    knows to skip its dynamic import on the server (the client picks\n    up the federated load during hydration). Without this guard, SSR\n    would error out trying to import a remote URL through Node''s\n    module loader.\n\ne2e.mjs:\n  Eight assertions covering the full round-trip: SSR login form,\n  signup, create note, edit title + body via the federated editor,\n  logout, re-login as same user, notes restored from DB, body\n  round-trips through DB, zero console errors. All pass.\n\nREADME.md documents the architecture, the auth model, the SSR flow,\nthe federation flow, and the testing approach.\n\nFramework tests still pass (80 unit + 70 conformance + types clean).","tree":{"sha":"38af0c267002b85a056c4983f22eece4c04c0cba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/38af0c267002b85a056c4983f22eece4c04c0cba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKDRjNGQ0YTY0NzQ3ZGJmOTE0M2MyOWFjOTA3ZTZlZWQ2YjNmMjVjZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57","sha":"fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57"}],"sha":"4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/4c4d4a64747dbf9143c29ac907e6eed6b3f25ced"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T18:11:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T18:11:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"federation: close three gaps — version, hot-reload primitive, devtools\n\nsrc/version.js:\n  VERSION constant + gte() lite-semver comparator. Suffixes like\n  -alpha are stripped for the core-version compare.\n\nloadFromManifest version enforcement:\n  When manifest.framework.minVersion is set, compare against ours.\n  onVersionMismatch: ''warn'' (default) | ''throw'' | ''silent''.\n\nreloadRemote(src):\n  Clears the in-flight import cache and calls .retry() on every\n  connected lazy placeholder for that src. Useful when the original\n  load failed (network, integrity, timeout) and the remote has come\n  back online. Returns the count of retried instances.\n\n  Documented limit: cannot swap a working component''s class. Custom\n  Elements registry is write-once per tag. True HMR would need a\n  fresh-tag-per-iteration scheme — explicit non-goal for now.\n\nframework-devtools custom element:\n  Drop on any page. Lists every federated tag, source URL, and live\n  instance count. Click a row to highlight instances on the page.\n  Renders in shadow DOM so its styles don''t leak. Re-polls every\n  500ms to pick up newly-registered components.\n\n  lazyComponent now tracks registry (tag -> { src, realTag,\n  registeredAt }) and liveInstances (src -> Set<LazyElement>) — both\n  exposed for devtools (and reloadRemote uses liveInstances).\n\nexamples/dashboard:\n  Drops <framework-devtools> on the page. The 100-cell grid shows up\n  in the panel with count 100; clicking highlights all instances with\n  a blue outline.\n\nFEDERATION.md:\n  Moved version / hot-reload / devtools to a ''Closed'' section.\n  Streaming SSR stitching remains the only open gap; documented as\n  a separate project rather than a small follow-up.\n\n80 unit (+8: version + reload + mismatch policies) + 70 conformance\ntests pass, types clean.","tree":{"sha":"049c90e6ab1fbf37d38f81bb8796c2dd19f2d321","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/049c90e6ab1fbf37d38f81bb8796c2dd19f2d321"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGZlOGIxZGYzNzkwYTY3YTc2ZDU2NmE4Njc0ODU5N2Q0YjFjODBhNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b","sha":"fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b"}],"sha":"fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fe8b1df3790a67a76d566a86748597d4b1c80a57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T17:11:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T17:11:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"styling demo + styleMap re-export + FEDERATION.md\n\nRe-export styleMap from lit-html (one line in index.js).\n\nexamples/styling/ — three side-by-side patterns on one page:\n  1. light DOM + page CSS\n  2. shadow: true + scoped <style>\n  3. reactive classMap + styleMap driven by signals\nVerified in chromium: light pill blue, shadow pill green (page''s\n.pill rule cannot reach into the shadow root), reactive hue cycles.\n\nframework/FEDERATION.md — authoritative doc on:\n  - what makes federation first-class (6 criteria + comparison\n    matrix against Webpack MF / single-spa / iframes / vanilla)\n  - extensibility matrix (DOM is universal; signals are our\n    extension)\n  - the platform bet on TC39 Signals\n  - honest gaps (hot reload, version enforcement, DevTools,\n    streaming SSR stitching)","tree":{"sha":"9373bd8f07c9682195dc1204e46f102714371694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/9373bd8f07c9682195dc1204e46f102714371694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGZkYWNmYzAzY2NkYTc3NjM2YzE2MDA3MzZmMTBhN2RkZTJlMmRkNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc","sha":"9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc"}],"sha":"fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/fdacfc03ccda77636c1600736f10a7dde2e2dd4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T16:47:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T16:47:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"federation: first-class error handling\n\nSix fixes addressing every silent-failure path in the federation\nplumbing.\n\nlazyComponent:\n  - Default onerror UI. On import failure (network, timeout, integrity\n    mismatch, missing-as-tag, origin refused) we now REPLACE the\n    fallback with a visible role=alert block including the URL, the\n    error message, and a Retry button. Previously the fallback\n    lingered forever.\n  - onerror({ src, error, retry }) => template, to override.\n  - timeout option (default 30_000ms; 0 disables). Races the import\n    against a timer so a hung CDN doesn''t leave the placeholder up\n    indefinitely.\n  - .retry() method on the element instance. Clears the shared\n    in-flight cache and re-runs #mount, so a transient failure can\n    recover without a page reload.\n\ndefineComponent:\n  - onError(err, host) => template option. A throw in setup() or in\n    the render function gets caught and the boundary renders in its\n    place. Without onError, errors are logged AND re-thrown (no\n    silent half-render).\n\nloadFromManifest:\n  - Return shape changed to { manifest, results: LoadResultEntry[] }.\n    Per-component failures (bad integrity format, etc.) are collected\n    instead of taking the whole manifest down.\n  - Each entry: { tag, status: ''registered''|''skipped''|''error'', reason? }\n  - Manifest-LEVEL errors (fetch failed, schema invalid) still throw.\n\nframework configure():\n  - configure({ singletonViolation: ''warn''|''throw''|''silent'' }).\n    Production code can opt the singleton check into throw so a\n    misconfigured federation fails loudly at boot rather than\n    producing dead reactivity later. Default remains ''warn'' so HMR\n    and tests don''t break.\n\nTests: 68 unit (+7 error-handling + manifest reshape) + 70 conformance\nall pass, types clean. New test/error-handling.test.js exercises every\nnew path.","tree":{"sha":"cf42f1171a596f33811c1c563006bbeb4b14a3d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/cf42f1171a596f33811c1c563006bbeb4b14a3d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKDlmOThiOTJmOGUyZmNmMDgxZDY1ZThlNTIyYTlhZTgyMjZjNWI2YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5","sha":"aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5"}],"sha":"9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/9f98b92f8e2fcf081d65e8e522a9ae8226c5b6bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T16:27:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T16:27:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"dashboard demo + federation manifest + manifest explorer\n\nThree deliverables in one commit, all reusing the same federation\nsubstrate.\n\nexamples/dashboard/\n  Federation perf stress test. 100-cell grid where each cell is a\n  federated <x-metric> loaded ONCE from examples/dashboard/widgets/\n  metric.js (a separate bundle path). Host owns shared signals:\n  playing / speedMultiplier / updateCount / fps. Each cell holds its\n  own value signal and updates on its own random 100-500ms interval,\n  scaled by the host''s speed slider. Pause/resume via the host\n  control.\n\n  Real numbers in chromium: 100 cells, sustained 60 FPS at 1×, still\n  60 FPS at 5× with ~2000 updates/sec. Lit''s diff + our signal core\n  handles it cleanly. Pause halts all cell intervals because the\n  effect re-binds on the playing signal.\n\nframework/src/manifest.js\n  Federation manifest format + loader. A remote serves a JSON file\n  at a known URL declaring the components it offers:\n\n    {\n      \"name\": \"acme-widgets\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n      \"framework\": { \"name\": \"mohsal-framework\", \"minVersion\": \"0.0.1\" },\n      \"components\": [{ \"tag\": \"acme-foo\", \"src\": \"./foo.js\", ... }]\n    }\n\n  loadFromManifest(url, { allowedOrigins, accept }) fetches it,\n  validates the schema (name/version/components/tag-has-hyphen),\n  resolves src URLs relative to the manifest, and registers every\n  component via lazyComponent with the supply-chain options forwarded\n  (integrity + allowedOrigins). The placeholder tag is `${tag}-lazy`\n  so templates read naturally:  <acme-foo-lazy></acme-foo-lazy>.\n\n  An optional accept() gate lets hosts skip components based on\n  version checks / feature flags / opt-outs — the host stays in\n  control of what actually loads.\n\nexamples/manifest/\n  Browser-side dev tool: paste a manifest URL, see what it offers,\n  live-preview each component. Uses loadFromManifest under the hood;\n  binds the dashboard''s widgets/manifest.json as a one-click sample\n  so the demo composes with the dashboard.\n\n61 unit (+6 manifest) + 70 conformance tests pass, types clean.\nAll six prior demos still work; the two new ones verified end-to-end.","tree":{"sha":"4afd458565a55a32806714bb707b33e7699b1d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/4afd458565a55a32806714bb707b33e7699b1d12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5","node_id":"C_kwDOSorhyNoAKGFjZWIwYzVhNmUyYjgwM2ExNzcxYmYwNjQyZmUwYzBjNDhhY2NkYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commit/300439febd4d5b439edaea2fd20e72f82875dcd0","sha":"300439febd4d5b439edaea2fd20e72f82875dcd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/300439febd4d5b439edaea2fd20e72f82875dcd0"}],"sha":"aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/aceb0c5a6e2b803a1771bf0642fe0c0c48accdc5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/commits/300439febd4d5b439edaea2fd20e72f82875dcd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T15:53:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T15:53:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"framework: complete migration to lit-html substrate\n\nAll examples + tests ported to the lit-html-based framework. Vendoring\nlit-html (~440KB on disk including source maps & d.ts) under\nframework/vendor/lit-html/ so consumers don''t need an import map and\nthe project stays zero-config: just load /framework/src/index.js.\n\nDemos ported and verified in chromium (zero console errors):\n  - homepage         x-work-board, classMap, repeat\n  - examples/todomvc TodoMVC with <x-todo-item> child component\n  - examples/router  routing as user-land signal + when()\n  - examples/federation host imports remote via lazyComponent, both\n                     share Signal.State across the bundle boundary\n  - examples/ssr     renderToString on happy-dom + browser hydration\n  - examples/security TT enforcement via lit-html policy\n\nFramework src: 7 files / 910 lines (was 12 files / 1506 lines, −40%).\nTests: 55 unit + 70 TC39 conformance, types clean.\n\nAPI changes from the previous self-built version:\n  on*=${fn}    → @event=${fn}      (lit-html event binding)\n  ${signal}    → ${signal.get()}    inside () => html\\`…\\`\n  class:foo    → classMap({ foo })\n  :value       → manual .value + @input  (recoverable as a directive)\n  unsafe()     → unsafeHTML directive\n  ref/repeat/when are re-exports of lit-html''s; same shape we had.\n\nComponent model:\n  defineComponent({ setup }) — setup may return:\n    (a) a function () => TemplateResult — wrapped in an effect, signal\n        reads inside re-render via lit-html diff (the common path);\n    (b) a TemplateResult — rendered once, no reactivity;\n    (c) null — leave host DOM intact (enhance mode).\n  observedAttributes + reactive props + emit + props bag unchanged.\n\nSecurity model rewritten in SECURITY.md to reflect substrate change:\n  - text interpolation safe-by-default (lit-html escapes)\n  - unsafeHTML is the explicit opt-in\n  - TT policy is \"lit-html\" (was \"mohsal-framework\")\n  - URL-scheme sanitization for href/src is now USER RESPONSIBILITY\n    (gap from the previous version; could be brought back as a tiny\n    safeURL directive if frequently hit)\n\nFederation primitives and SSR pipeline unchanged in behaviour — the\nsubstrate swap was purely at the templating layer, as discussed.\n\nThe deleted LIT_POC_FINDINGS.md, having served its purpose, is gone.","tree":{"sha":"2eb9cf14eeaf486eda5d752c16ebde401f87a4ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/trees/2eb9cf14eeaf486eda5d752c16ebde401f87a4ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mohsalsaleem/salmo/git/commits/300439febd4d5b439edaea2fd20e72f82875dcd0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/oth