rs/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/031881dd5f9c5919178abe4d6bfcc07a6a8607e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:15:45Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:15:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dismiss failed approvals and accept every country as a builder location (#264)\n\nApprovals whose publishing failed had no way out: they could not be\nrejected, reopened or revoked, and retrying failed again on the same data.\nAdmins can now dismiss them from the review sheet or from Chief. The record\nmoves to rejected with a failure_dismissed audit entry, leaves the failed\nqueue and digest, and stays reopenable. The submitter is not notified.\n\nBuilder locations were limited to a 33-country shortlist, so approvals such\nas \"Iraq\" failed to publish. The list now covers every country, with common\nalternate names and accent-insensitive matching.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e93ebf3c4bc64027486b115c7016e3f58719544a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/git/trees/e93ebf3c4bc64027486b115c7016e3f58719544a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/git/commits/031881dd5f9c5919178abe4d6bfcc07a6a8607e6","verification":{"payload":"tree e93ebf3c4bc64027486b115c7016e3f58719544a\nparent 26c4f3138c87b95e601efce9c5b9cb1f43b13ceb\nauthor Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com> 1791299745 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791299745 +0500\n\nDismiss failed approvals and accept every country as a builder location (#264)\n\nApprovals whose publishing failed had no way out: they could not be\nrejected, reopened or revoked, and retrying failed again on the same data.\nAdmins can now dismiss them from the review sheet or from Chief. The record\nmoves to rejected with a failure_dismissed audit entry, leaves the failed\nqueue and digest, and stays reopenable. The submitter is not notified.\n\nBuilder locations were limited to a 33-country shortlist, so approvals such\nas \"Iraq\" failed to publish. The list now covers every country, with common\nalternate names and accent-insensitive matching.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRChCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+pAQAF349XTznntEUFPHpSznq4tw\nGDr9zbCkVXISUWl+eSj1mXzBPJZbPYykUHZ4CxOhpop/TixKvZV6Y5l//rVPSK3Q\nK52Q/U0xo97TLs2H97elyMhGm7sgDNS8R0cVRPABzq0mAECIAS33vU+Gc21fhdDf\nMrYxy+TBy391P76nayz3ezBTbkbft4rxyJeOxn9p1BbebUePquiYlquug4cRFgtr\nHLkjF81Ei4fCUOpujzofAPICd1bhqxNGI6qsSjcv3C48p8XRXo/QJGYSymBFgtWA\nIIouxDqMK0iGh4c+HY09g6oFWtj71gdWjjip3qZoKyCcZ4o8R39ri4903iRgodu6\nSfFUm5afyVhznM7DBPx/ca+7Fcapv9IG8EgMySxs0ul2vvGjzPN/ZkesT7ya6zDO\nJ2bcs6jC1F6TuZTmfK6pQ3ytgscmaLBNuasrdRxFDL8nV4/6pdr82gGMc5vjG0t6\nlRbatvOLU+A7LJMzLvKi6jEdRUy8Y78dO64dxNJtj++1ef6TW5E14x37WDVnDo1y\ny1JnKr/SRvPC8Uec06/4skQqJ5V9P/PuhIX9GAkDV8BQv5vGk4T85lBDpTlVlDMi\n4Bjo/YYDjvIj4eck5N7bzlb1FQNA5GKQQeKf1GVlsGKHjuLJxGn0R1P7z93aBcNf\nLWb50Wa9LfdiWjKMwfAX\n=9wly\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:15:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commit/031881dd5f9c5919178abe4d6bfcc07a6a8607e6","node_id":"C_kwDOSoxJW9oAKDAzMTg4MWRkNWY5YzU5MTkxNzhhYmU0ZDZiZmNjMDdhNmE4NjA3ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commit/26c4f3138c87b95e601efce9c5b9cb1f43b13ceb","sha":"26c4f3138c87b95e601efce9c5b9cb1f43b13ceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/26c4f3138c87b95e601efce9c5b9cb1f43b13ceb"}],"sha":"031881dd5f9c5919178abe4d6bfcc07a6a8607e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/031881dd5f9c5919178abe4d6bfcc07a6a8607e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165388405?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/saadiqbal-dev","id":165388405,"login":"saadiqbal-dev","node_id":"U_kgDOCdugdQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saadiqbal-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/26c4f3138c87b95e601efce9c5b9cb1f43b13ceb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:00:01Z","email":"saadiqbal.dev@outlook.com","name":"SloppyDev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:00:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Admin review digest, NEAR AI evaluation, and Telegram review via Chief (#263)\n\n* feat: admin review digest, Claude evaluation, and Telegram review via Chief\n\n- Evaluate pending submissions at submission time with deterministic checks\n  plus a Claude assessment (ready / review / spam), stored per submission\n  and shown in the admin dashboard with a Re-evaluate action.\n- GET /reviews/digest (reviews:read) feeds the daily Telegram digest.\n- POST /reviews/telegram-decision (reviews:write) lets admins approve or\n  reject from Telegram, recorded under their own linked account.\n- Telegram linking: one-time /link codes, /admin/telegram-link confirm page,\n  and a Telegram tab in the admin dashboard to remove access.\n- Proposals migrations 0001-0003 (additive only).\n- New API secrets: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN (optional).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: tighten review API access and Telegram linking\n\n- Review API keys no longer count as admins when reading proposals. The\n  digest reads through the in-process evaluator context instead, so the bot\n  key can no longer fetch raw payloads (including private queues) from\n  GET /proposals or the audit log.\n- Telegram decisions look up the proposal by id instead of scanning the\n  first 500 pending items.\n- POST /reviews/telegram-links returns only alreadyLinked, not which admin\n  account a Telegram ID belongs to.\n- The link confirm page warns when confirming replaces the admin''s existing\n  link to a different Telegram account, and no longer names the admin''s own\n  account as the current owner.\n- evaluatorContext moved to its own review-context module.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(proposals): squash migrations 0001-0003 into a single migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: trim review digest, sweep and Telegram review code\n\n- Derive digest types from ReviewDigestSchema and share one plugin id list\n- Share a collectPages helper between the digest and the sweep\n- Reuse one verdict enum and pick the digest evaluation schema\n- Inline Telegram reviewer pass-throughs and the usage logging hook\n- Look up the linked reviewer inside decideTelegramReview\n- Drop the duplicate source label in the evaluation panel\n- Share setup helpers in the Telegram review and sweep tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review on PR #263\n\n- Link flow flipped: admins create a one-time code in the dashboard''s\n  Telegram tab and send it to Chief, so a /link URL can no longer be used to\n  phish an admin into linking someone else''s Telegram. Removes the confirm\n  page and its preview.\n- Telegram decisions and link claims require the API key to belong to an\n  admin account; each decision logs the key id.\n- Link-code creation and linking run in transactions; a concurrent link for\n  the same admin returns a clear CONFLICT instead of a 500.\n- Evaluation sweep retries an item at most five times with backoff, whether\n  the save fails or Claude keeps refusing.\n- Claude calls time out after 60 seconds.\n- Check details are clamped to 500 characters; evaluation source limit\n  matches POST /proposals (100).\n- Digest and sweep fetch evaluations in batches of 500.\n- Removed the unused POST /reviews/evaluate endpoint.\n- Changeset updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): evaluate submissions with NEAR AI Cloud instead of the Anthropic API\n\nReplace the Anthropic SDK assessor with a fetch-based client for the NEAR AI\nCloud OpenAI-compatible chat completions API, using a strict JSON schema\nresponse format. The secret is now NEARAI_API_KEY and the default model is\nz-ai/glm-5.3-flash (TEE-hosted); reviewEvaluationModel still overrides it.\nDrops the @anthropic-ai/sdk dependency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): allow choosing the review model with NEARAI_MODEL\n\nNEARAI_MODEL, when set, overrides the reviewEvaluationModel variable so the\nmodel can be switched per environment without republishing config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6014cef1fa6db5779e0d55743ce2e96005baba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/git/trees/f6014cef1fa6db5779e0d55743ce2e96005baba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/git/commits/26c4f3138c87b95e601efce9c5b9cb1f43b13ceb","verification":{"payload":"tree f6014cef1fa6db5779e0d55743ce2e96005baba7\nparent 8cb5ed10d167c26f80aae0ef5ae4bcc5b0835f1c\nauthor SloppyDev <saadiqbal.dev@outlook.com> 1791295201 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791295201 +0500\n\nAdmin review digest, NEAR AI evaluation, and Telegram review via Chief (#263)\n\n* feat: admin review digest, Claude evaluation, and Telegram review via Chief\n\n- Evaluate pending submissions at submission time with deterministic checks\n  plus a Claude assessment (ready / review / spam), stored per submission\n  and shown in the admin dashboard with a Re-evaluate action.\n- GET /reviews/digest (reviews:read) feeds the daily Telegram digest.\n- POST /reviews/telegram-decision (reviews:write) lets admins approve or\n  reject from Telegram, recorded under their own linked account.\n- Telegram linking: one-time /link codes, /admin/telegram-link confirm page,\n  and a Telegram tab in the admin dashboard to remove access.\n- Proposals migrations 0001-0003 (additive only).\n- New API secrets: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN (optional).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: tighten review API access and Telegram linking\n\n- Review API keys no longer count as admins when reading proposals. The\n  digest reads through the in-process evaluator context instead, so the bot\n  key can no longer fetch raw payloads (including private queues) from\n  GET /proposals or the audit log.\n- Telegram decisions look up the proposal by id instead of scanning the\n  first 500 pending items.\n- POST /reviews/telegram-links returns only alreadyLinked, not which admin\n  account a Telegram ID belongs to.\n- The link confirm page warns when confirming replaces the admin''s existing\n  link to a different Telegram account, and no longer names the admin''s own\n  account as the current owner.\n- evaluatorContext moved to its own review-context module.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(proposals): squash migrations 0001-0003 into a single migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: trim review digest, sweep and Telegram review code\n\n- Derive digest types from ReviewDigestSchema and share one plugin id list\n- Share a collectPages helper between the digest and the sweep\n- Reuse one verdict enum and pick the digest evaluation schema\n- Inline Telegram reviewer pass-throughs and the usage logging hook\n- Look up the linked reviewer inside decideTelegramReview\n- Drop the duplicate source label in the evaluation panel\n- Share setup helpers in the Telegram review and sweep tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review on PR #263\n\n- Link flow flipped: admins create a one-time code in the dashboard''s\n  Telegram tab and send it to Chief, so a /link URL can no longer be used to\n  phish an admin into linking someone else''s Telegram. Removes the confirm\n  page and its preview.\n- Telegram decisions and link claims require the API key to belong to an\n  admin account; each decision logs the key id.\n- Link-code creation and linking run in transactions; a concurrent link for\n  the same admin returns a clear CONFLICT instead of a 500.\n- Evaluation sweep retries an item at most five times with backoff, whether\n  the save fails or Claude keeps refusing.\n- Claude calls time out after 60 seconds.\n- Check details are clamped to 500 characters; evaluation source limit\n  matches POST /proposals (100).\n- Digest and sweep fetch evaluations in batches of 500.\n- Removed the unused POST /reviews/evaluate endpoint.\n- Changeset updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): evaluate submissions with NEAR AI Cloud instead of the Anthropic API\n\nReplace the Anthropic SDK assessor with a fetch-based client for the NEAR AI\nCloud OpenAI-compatible chat completions API, using a strict JSON schema\nresponse format. The secret is now NEARAI_API_KEY and the default model is\nz-ai/glm-5.3-flash (TEE-hosted); reviewEvaluationModel still overrides it.\nDrops the @anthropic-ai/sdk dependency.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): allow choosing the review model with NEARAI_MODEL\n\nNEARAI_MODEL, when set, overrides the reviewEvaluationModel variable so the\nmodel can be switched per environment without republishing config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxP7hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5ekQAGMNJCJz0FxQ5E0EeCmzK3qC\nMvAwS2wTjyROl71A4FYeB4VXt39TpKvpIBv9QCkyMIw6IMVJSbT8b+ctgojWF+EZ\nTiEAzjxf4bejFzw+Jtp8oR4USZu3F35m9k6lHH0QMrD9U3aO2VZGM6yArbI+vooD\nbE/7VRmEOC0B5nRGXUK0A9QtlIV7x/GyzDCcFI8oeGo6syS/++tC8X/2qmVmbCfZ\nSftoV//dUBd0