ps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commit/db1f562ff3e6c6e6a20bde8f196693dec8dda2dd","node_id":"C_kwDOSoxJW9oAKGRiMWY1NjJmZjNlNmM2ZTZhMjBiZGU4ZjE5NjY5M2RlYzhkZGEyZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commit/5960b9fe51d9e195535cf96af98d1c3ceff054de","sha":"5960b9fe51d9e195535cf96af98d1c3ceff054de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/5960b9fe51d9e195535cf96af98d1c3ceff054de"}],"sha":"db1f562ff3e6c6e6a20bde8f196693dec8dda2dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/db1f562ff3e6c6e6a20bde8f196693dec8dda2dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/commits/5960b9fe51d9e195535cf96af98d1c3ceff054de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:12:14Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:12:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(admin): split dashboard into nested TanStack Router routes (#207)\n\n* resolve\n\n* refactor(admin): split dashboard into nested TanStack Router routes\n\nThe admin dashboard previously lived at /admin/dashboard and managed tab\nstate in URL search params. X nominations lived at a separate\n/admin/nominations page with no link from the dashboard chrome.\n\nTurn the dashboard into a real layout with sibling routes, matching the\nidiomatic TanStack Router pattern used elsewhere in the app\n(_authenticated/_dashboard/):\n\n  /admin/dashboard                  layout\n  /admin/dashboard/                 index → /admin/dashboard/builders\n  /admin/dashboard/builders         Builders tab (was dashboard/tab=builders)\n  /admin/dashboard/projects         Projects tab\n  /admin/dashboard/events           Events tab\n  /admin/dashboard/activity         Activity tab\n  /admin/dashboard/x-nominations    X nominations (was /admin/nominations)\n\nEach tab is now deep-linkable; browser back/forward switches tabs;\ndefaultPreload: \"intent\" already at ui/src/router.tsx:78 handles tab\npreloading automatically.\n\nNew shared <ProposalTab pluginId search actions> extracted to\n-proposal-tab.tsx and used by the four proposal leaves. Each leaf\nconstructs the typed setQuery/setStatus/setSelectedItem callbacks via\nuseNavigate({ from: Route.fullPath }), keeping navigation type-safe\ninside the leaf without coupling the shared component to a single\nroute.\n\nLayout assets:\n- header H1, five-tab <Link> nav with intent preload and active styling\n- useQueries for the four proposal pending counts\n- useQuery against builders.getXNominationMetrics() for the X nominations\n  pending badge (pendingReviewCount from\n  plugins/builders/src/services/x-nomination-admin.ts:66)\n- orpc.subscribeProposals live SSE subscription + invalidation, kept at\n  the layout so all tabs refetch together\n\nOther changes:\n- -proposal-dashboard.ts: replace DASHBOARD_TABS / getPluginId /\n  parseDashboardSearch with ADMIN_TABS, ProposalTabSearch,\n  parseProposalTabSearch\n- nominations.tsx deleted; -nominations-search.ts kept\n- user-nav.tsx: admin dropdown now links to /admin/dashboard/builders\n- generated ui/src/routeTree.gen.ts: new routes\n\nTests pass (ui + all plugins), biome clean. The 2 pre-existing typecheck\nerrors in member-card.tsx and auth-types.gen.ts are not touched by this\nbranch.\n\n* wip\n\n* refactor(admin): unify dashboard filter bar, table, pagination, and loaders\n\nAlign all five admin dashboard tabs (Builders, Projects, Events,\nActivity, X Nominations) around shared primitives:\n\n- New FilterBar and RecordsState primitives under _admin/admin/ for\n  per-tab header and empty/error panels with shared copy templates.\n- New polymorphism-style <DataTable<T>> wrapping the react-table\n  chrome shared by ProposalTable and XNominationTable.\n- Per-tab noun ({ singular, plural }) drives every visible copy\n  surface: subtitle, loading state, search placeholder, empty title,\n  error title.\n- Auto-fetch infinite scroll on every tab; the proposal tabs drop\n  the Load more button.\n- CSV export unified on disabled-when-empty + loading-during-in-flight\n  for all tabs.\n- Each tab route gains a TanStack Router loader that\n  prefetchInfiniteQuery''s the first page into the cache.\n- /admin redirects to /admin/dashboard via _admin/admin/index.tsx.\n\nDrops the X Nominations ''pending_contact'' default, unused exports\n(NominationsSearch type, Noun type), and duplicated titleCase\nhelpers.\n\n* chore(deps): bump better-near-auth, every-plugin, everything-dev\n\n- better-near-auth 1.8.2 → 1.10.0\n- every-plugin 2.10.0 → 2.10.1\n- everything-dev 1.52.0 → 1.53.0\n\nUpdates package.json catalog and bun.lock to match.\n\n* chore: update env template, bos/docker config, and ui app entry\n\n- Restructure .env.example to group keys by component (app.host,\n  app.api, app.auth, plugins.*) and add placeholders for auth and\n  new integrations (resend, twilio, fastnear, NEAR relayer, etc.).\n- Drop the stale production deployment entries from bos.config.json\n  (no longer tracked via zephyrcloud URLs); keep local dev config.\n- Renumber docker compose database ports to reflect the current\n  plugin layout.\n- Update ui/src/app.ts entry to export the new sessionQueryKey helper\n  alongside sessionQueryOptions.\n- Regenerate ui/src/routeTree.gen.ts from the router source.\n\n* upgrade\n\n* lock\n\n* fix tests","tree":{"sha":"ea18d9d4c3886da8e91261788ea16baaa892eb46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/git/trees/ea18d9d4c3886da8e91261788ea16baaa892eb46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org/git/commits/5960b9fe51d9e195535cf96af98d1c3ceff054de","verification":{"payload":"tree ea18d9d4c3886da8e91261788ea16baaa892eb46\nparent fbf1d18eb491dbbecd6464f6fb7906dadc86fc29\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1787091134 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787091134 -0500\n\nrefactor(admin): split dashboard into nested TanStack Router routes (#207)\n\n* resolve\n\n* refactor(admin): split dashboard into nested TanStack Router routes\n\nThe admin dashboard previously lived at /admin/dashboard and managed tab\nstate in URL search params. X nominations lived at a separate\n/admin/nominations page with no link from the dashboard chrome.\n\nTurn the dashboard into a real layout with sibling routes, matching the\nidiomatic TanStack Router pattern used elsewhere in the app\n(_authenticated/_dashboard/):\n\n  /admin/dashboard                  layout\n  /admin/dashboard/                 index → /admin/dashboard/builders\n  /admin/dashboard/builders         Builders tab (was dashboard/tab=builders)\n  /admin/dashboard/projects         Projects tab\n  /admin/dashboard/events           Events tab\n  /admin/dashboard/activity         Activity tab\n  /admin/dashboard/x-nominations    X nominations (was /admin/nominations)\n\nEach tab is now deep-linkable; browser back/forward switches tabs;\ndefaultPreload: \"intent\" already at ui/src/router.tsx:78 handles tab\npreloading automatically.\n\nNew shared <ProposalTab pluginId search actions> extracted to\n-proposal-tab.tsx and used by the four proposal leaves. Each leaf\nconstructs the typed setQuery/setStatus/setSelectedItem callbacks via\nuseNavigate({ from: Route.fullPath }), keeping navigation type-safe\ninside the leaf without coupling the shared component to a single\nroute.\n\nLayout assets:\n- header H1, five-tab <Link> nav with intent preload and active styling\n- useQueries for the four proposal pending counts\n- useQuery against builders.getXNominationMetrics() for the X nominations\n  pending badge (pendingReviewCount from\n  plugins/builders/src/services/x-nomination-admin.ts:66)\n- orpc.subscribeProposals live SSE subscription + invalidation, kept at\n  the layout so all tabs refetch together\n\nOther changes:\n- -proposal-dashboard.ts: replace DASHBOARD_TABS / getPluginId /\n  parseDashboardSearch with ADMIN_TABS, ProposalTabSearch,\n  parseProposalTabSearch\n- nominations.tsx deleted; -nominations-search.ts kept\n- user-nav.tsx: admin dropdown now links to /admin/dashboard/builders\n- generated ui/src/routeTree.gen.ts: new routes\n\nTests pass (ui + all plugins), biome clean. The 2 pre-existing typecheck\nerrors in member-card.tsx and auth-types.gen.ts are not touched by this\nbranch.\n\n* wip\n\n* refactor(admin): unify dashboard filter bar, table, pagination, and loaders\n\nAlign all five admin dashboard tabs (Builders, Projects, Events,\nActivity, X Nominations) around shared primitives:\n\n- New FilterBar and RecordsState primitives under _admin/admin/ for\n  per-tab header and empty/error panels with shared copy templates.\n- New polymorphism-style <DataTable<T>> wrapping the react-table\n  chrome shared by ProposalTable and XNominationTable.\n- Per-tab noun ({ singular, plural }) drives every visible copy\n  surface: subtitle, loading state, search placeholder, empty title,\n  error title.\n- Auto-fetch infinite scroll on every tab; the proposal tabs drop\n  the Load more button.\n- CSV export unified on disabled-when-empty + loading-during-in-flight\n  for all tabs.\n- Each tab route gains a TanStack Router loader that\n  prefetchInfiniteQuery''s the first page into the cache.\n- /admin redirects to /admin/dashboard via _admin/admin/index.tsx.\n\nDrops the X Nominations ''pending_contact'' default, unused exports\n(NominationsSearch type, Noun type), and duplicated titleCase\nhelpers.\n\n* chore(deps): bump better-near-auth, every-plugin, everything-dev\n\n- better-near-auth 1.8.2 → 1.10.0\n- every-plugin 2.10.0 → 2.10.1\n- everything-dev 1.52.0 → 1.53.0\n\nUpdates package.json catalog and bun.lock to match.\n\n* chore: update env template, bos/docker config, and ui app entry\n\n- Restructure .env.example to group keys by component (app.host,\n  app.api, app.auth, plugins.*) and add placeholders for auth and\n  new integrations (resend, twilio, fastnear, NEAR relayer, etc.).\n- Drop the stale production deployment entries from bos.config.json\n  (no longer tracked via zephyrcloud URLs); keep local dev config.\n- Renumber docker compose database ports to reflect the current\n  plugin layout.\n- Update ui/src/app.ts entry to export the new sessionQueryKey helper\n  alongside sessionQueryOptions.\n- Regenerate ui/src/routeTree.gen.ts from the router source.\n\n* upgrade\n\n* lock\n\n* fix tests","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhNi+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZU8QAGjLVH9XtJyJIFt2vpV7sVy9\nB+Ul4uaBVGhnAqBFFxZ9yzQ5SeluP4oNLLvqpYxG0T2YeXpIcIusWHWY5ydpqGR